+# Scene-Referred HDR Path — Pipeline Audit
+
+Status: research (read-only audit), 2026-08-28
+
+Scope: CRYENGINE 5.7.1 source at `E:\coding3\ReC_sandbox\CRYENGINE_Source`, as modified by the
+CinematicCamera work already present in this repo. Every claim carries a `file:line` citation
+against the working tree at the time of the audit; where something could not be determined from
+the source it is marked **UNKNOWN**. Paths are given relative to the repo root
+`E:\coding3\ReC_sandbox\CRYENGINE_Source\`. No file other than this report was modified.
+
+---
+
+## A. Render-target formats and precision
+
+### A0. The three format-selection helpers
+
+| Helper | Definition | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| `CRendererResources::GetHDRFormat(withAlpha, lowQuality)` | `Code/CryEngine/RenderDll/Common/RendererResources.cpp:428-441` | `eTF_R16G16B16A16F`, downgraded to `eTF_R11G11B10F` when `!withAlpha` and the quality rules below permit |
+| `CRendererResources::GetLDRFormat(precisionBits)` | `Common/RendererResources.cpp:443-451` | `eTF_R8G8B8A8`, or `eTF_R10G10B10A2` when `precisionBits` |
+| `CRendererResources::GetDisplayFormat()` | `Common/RendererResources.cpp:453-458` | always `eTF_R8G8B8A8` |
+
+`GetHDRFormat` body (`Common/RendererResources.cpp:430-440`):
+
+```cpp
+ETEX_Format candidate = eTF_R16G16B16A16F;
+if (!withAlpha && s_hwTexFormatSupport.IsFormatSupported(eTF_R11G11B10F))
+{
+    if (CRenderer::CV_r_HDRTexFormat <= 1 && lowQuality)
+        candidate = eTF_R11G11B10F;
+    if (CRenderer::CV_r_HDRTexFormat <= 0)
+        candidate = eTF_R11G11B10F;
+}
+return candidate;
+```
+
+`r_HDRTexFormat` is registered at `Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1192-1198` with **default 1**
+("standard precision"); its change callback (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:705-711`) only releases
+permanent render objects.
+
+With stock cvars:
+
+* `nHDRFormat  = GetHDRFormat(false, false)` → **`eTF_R16G16B16A16F`**
+* `nHDRAFormat = GetHDRFormat(true , false)` → **`eTF_R16G16B16A16F`** (alpha forces fp16)
+* `nHDRQFormat = GetHDRFormat(false, true )` → **`eTF_R11G11B10F`**  ← the lossy one
+* `nLDRPFormat = GetLDRFormat(true)`         → **`eTF_R10G10B10A2`** (UNORM, clamps to `[0,1]`)
+
+ETEX → DXGI, `XRenderD3D9/DeviceManager/DeviceFormats.cpp`:
+
+* `:86`  `m_FormatR8G8B8A8.CheckSupport(DXGI_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM, "R8G8B8A8")`
+* `:102` `m_FormatR11G11B10F.CheckSupport(DXGI_FORMAT_R11G11B10_FLOAT, "R11G11B10F")`
+* `:103` `m_FormatR10G10B10A2.CheckSupport(DXGI_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UNORM, "R10G10B10A2")`
+* `:104` `m_FormatR16G16B16A16.CheckSupport(DXGI_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_UNORM, "R16G16B16A16")`
+* `:106` `m_FormatR16G16B16A16F.CheckSupport(DXGI_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_FLOAT, "R16G16B16A16F")`
+
+`R11G11B10_FLOAT` has **no sign bit** and 6/6/5 mantissa bits: every negative value is clamped to
+0 on write. This is the single most important precision fact in the current pipeline.
+
+### A1. Every HDR / post render target
+
+Created in `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/Common/GraphicsPipeline.cpp`,
+`CGraphicsPipelineResources::CreateHDRMaps()` at `:208-271`.
+
+| Target (member) | Line | Size | Format (default cvars) | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `m_pTexHDRTarget` (`$HDRTarget`) | `:221` | full | **R16G16B16A16F** | UAV; written by tiled shading |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetScaled[0][0]` (`$HDRTarget 1/2a`) | `:224` | 1/2 | R16G16B16A16F | bloom / sun-shafts source |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetScaled[1][0]` (`$HDRTarget 1/4a`) | `:225` | 1/4 | R16G16B16A16F | bloom / auto-exposure source |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetScaled[1][1]` (`$HDRTarget 1/4b`) | `:226` | 1/4 | R16G16B16A16F | bloom ping-pong |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetMaskedScaled[0][0..3]` | `:229-232` | 1/2 | R16G16B16A16F (`nHDRAFormat`) | DOF near/far layers |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetMaskedScaled[1][0..1]` | `:233-234` | 1/4 | R16G16B16A16F | |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetMaskedScaled[2][0..1]` | `:235-236` | 1/8 | R16G16B16A16F | |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetMaskedScaled[3][0..1]` | `:237-238` | 1/16 | R16G16B16A16F | |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetPrev[0]` (`$HDRTargetPrev_Left`) | `:239` | full | **R11G11B10F** (`nHDRQFormat`) | **lossy**; read by SSR, water, motion blur |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetPrev[1]` (`$HDRTargetPrev_Right`) | `:240` | full | **R11G11B10F** | |
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetMasked` (`$HDRTargetMasked`) | `:241` | full | R16G16B16A16F | |
+| `m_pTexSceneTargetR11G11B10F[0]` | `:243` | full | **R11G11B10F** | heavily shared — see below |
+| `m_pTexSceneTargetR11G11B10F[1]` | `:244` | full | **R11G11B10F** | |
+| `m_pTexHDRFinalBloom` (`$HDRFinalBloom`) | `:246` | 1/4 | **R11G11B10F** (`nHDRQFormat`) | **the bloom result is R11G11B10F** |
+| `m_pTexVelocity` | `:248` | full | eTF_R8G8B8A8 | motion vectors, not colour |
+| `m_pTexVelocityTiles[0..2]` | `:249-251` | tile | eTF_R8G8B8A8 | not colour |
+| `m_pTexSceneCoCTemp` / `m_pTexSceneCoC[i]` | `:254`, `:259` | 1/2… | eTF_R16G16F | CoC, not colour |
+| `m_pTexHDRMeasuredLuminance[i]` | `:266` | 1×1 | eTF_R16G16F | (luminance, illuminance) |
+
+**`m_pTexSceneTargetR11G11B10F[]` is the most heavily shared lossy buffer in the pipeline.** Its
+consumers, all working in R11G11B10F:
+
+* **Subsurface scattering** — the tiled-shading compute writes the SSS diffuse accumulation into
+  `[0]` as a UAV (`XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/TiledShading.cpp:121`
+  `SetOutputUAV(2, …m_pTexSceneTargetR11G11B10F[0]);`, matching `TiledShading.cfi:1068`
+  `DiffuseAccUAV[pixelCoord] = float3( diffuseAcc );`), and `CScreenSpaceSSSStage` blurs through
+  `[1]` (`ScreenSpaceSSS.cpp:28`, `:57`).
+* **Lens optics / flares** — `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/LensOptics.cpp:29` renders into `[0]`,
+  read back by the PostAA composite at `PostAA.cpp:401`.
+* **Water caustics** — `Water.cpp:593` writes `[1]`, consumed by `TiledShading.cpp:97`.
+* **Motion blur** — the copy at `MotionBlur.cpp:185` and the read at `:201`.
+
+Other colour targets:
+
+* `m_pTexSceneTarget` (`$SceneTarget`) — `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:313`, full res,
+  `eHDRTF = GetHDRFormat(false,false)` → **R16G16B16A16F**. DOF/refraction scratch.
+* `m_pTexDisplayTargetSrc` / `m_pTexDisplayTargetDst` — `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:294` / `:295`,
+  full res, `nLDRPFormat` = **eTF_R10G10B10A2 (UNORM)**. *This is the tone-mapper's output
+  target, so everything past the tone-map is hard-clamped to `[0,1]` in 10 bits.*
+* `m_pTexDisplayTargetScaled[0..2]` — `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:289-291`, `nLDRPFormat`
+  (**R10G10B10A2 UNORM**). **The sun-shafts stage uses these as its working buffers**
+  (`XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/SunShafts.cpp:36-43`), so sun shafts are computed in a UNORM
+  `[0,1]` buffer.
+* `m_pTexDisplayTargetScaledTemp[0..1]` — `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:297-298`, same UNORM format.
+* `m_pTexWaterVolumeRefl[0..1]` — `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:300-301`, `nHDRQFormat` → R11G11B10F.
+* G-buffer `$SceneNormalsMap` / `$SceneDiffuse` / `$SceneSpecular` — `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:141-143`,
+  all `eTF_R8G8B8A8` with `FT_USAGE_ALLOWREADSRGB`.
+* HUD `m_pTexHUD3D[0..1]` — `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:337`, `:349`, `eTF_R8G8B8A8`.
+
+Auto-exposure ladder (still allocated by the legacy resource manager):
+
+* `CRendererResources::s_ptexHDRAdaptedLuminanceCur[0..7]` — 1×1, `eTF_R16G16F`,
+  `Common/RendererResources.cpp:571-572`.
+* `CRendererResources::s_ptexHDRToneMaps[i]` (`$HDRToneMap_i`) — `4^i` square, `eTF_R16G16F`,
+  `Common/RendererResources.cpp:582-584`. Index 0 is 1×1 and carries `FT_STAGE_READBACK`.
+
+**PostAA history ("prev back buffer") targets** — `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/PostAA.cpp:622-656`:
+
+```cpp
+ETEX_Format accumulatorFormat = eTF_R16G16B16A16;                 // PostAA.cpp:627  (UNORM!)
+if (CRenderer::CV_r_AntialiasingMode <= eAT_SMAA_2TX && CRendererCVars::CV_r_HDRTexFormat == 0)
+    accumulatorFormat = eTF_R10G10B10A2;                          // PostAA.cpp:628-629
+```
+
+`$PrevBackBuffer0/1` (`PostAA.cpp:641-642`, `_R` variants `:647-649`) are therefore
+**DXGI_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_UNORM** — 16 bits but still clamped to `[0,1]`. Harmless today
+because PostAA runs after tone-mapping; a hard blocker for HDR post-AA.
+
+Formats that lose sign and/or range, summarised:
+
+* **R11G11B10F (no sign, low mantissa):** `m_pTexHDRTargetPrev[]`, `m_pTexSceneTargetR11G11B10F[]`,
+  `m_pTexHDRFinalBloom`, `m_pTexWaterVolumeRefl[]`.
+* **R10G10B10A2 UNORM (`[0,1]` clamp):** `m_pTexDisplayTargetSrc/Dst`,
+  `m_pTexDisplayTargetScaled[]`, `m_pTexDisplayTargetScaledTemp[]` — i.e. the whole LDR stage
+  *and* the sun-shafts working set.
+* **R16G16B16A16 UNORM (`[0,1]` clamp):** PostAA history buffers.
+* **R8G8B8A8:** G-buffer, HUD, velocity, colour chart, swapchain.
+
+### A2. Backbuffer / swapchain format and colour space
+
+`CSwapChain::GetSwapChainFormat()` — `Common/SwapChain.cpp:38-72`:
+
+```cpp
+//	TODO: Activate once sRGB encoding is gone from the shader           // SwapChain.cpp:40
+DXGI_FORMAT fmt = DXGI_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM;                           // SwapChain.cpp:53
+switch (CRendererCVars::CV_r_HDRSwapChain)
+{
+case 0: fmt = DXGI_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM /*_SRGB*/; break;              // SwapChain.cpp:57
+case 1: fmt = DXGI_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_UNORM; break;                    // SwapChain.cpp:58
+case 2: fmt = DXGI_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_FLOAT; break;                    // SwapChain.cpp:59
+#if defined(__dxgi1_5_h__) || false /* TODO */
+case 3..9: /* BT.709 / BT.2020 variants */                              // SwapChain.cpp:61-67
+#endif
+}
+```
+
+**`r_HDRSwapChain` is never registered as a cvar.** Both `REGISTER_CVAR3("r_HDRSwapChain", …)`
+calls sit inside an `#if 0` opened at `Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1161-1163`
+(`// TODO: Activate once sRGB encoding is gone from the shader`) and closed at `:1190`; the
+registrations themselves are at `:1165` and `:1174`. The variable is a zero-initialised static
+(`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:185`, declared `Common/RendererCVars.h:248`), so
+`CV_r_HDRSwapChain == 0` always and the swapchain is **`DXGI_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM` — non-sRGB,
+plain 8-bit UNORM**.
+
+Consequences:
+
+* No HDR swapchain is reachable at runtime. Cases 3–9 are behind a second
+  `#if defined(__dxgi1_5_h__)` guard as well.
+* Platform overrides: Durango `R8G8B8A8_UNORM` (`SwapChain.cpp:46`); **GNM/PS4 is the only sRGB
+  swapchain** — `SwapChain.cpp:49` `DXGI_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM_SRGB`; SDL2 `B8G8R8X8_UNORM`
+  (`SwapChain.cpp:51`).
+* Applied at `Common/SwapChain.cpp:85` (`scDesc.BufferDesc.Format = GetSwapChainFormat();`) and
+  `:171` (`swapChainDesc.Format = …`).
+* `CSwapChainBackedRenderDisplayContext::AllocateBackBuffers()` sets the proxy's `SRGBRead` flag
+  by comparing the display format's sRGB twin against the swapchain surface format —
+  `Common/RenderDisplayContext.cpp:286` and per-buffer at `:308` — which with a UNORM chain
+  evaluates **false**.
+* `Common/RenderDisplayContext.h:103` `GetColorFormat()` → `GetDisplayFormat()` → `eTF_R8G8B8A8`;
+  `Common/RenderDisplayContext.h:100` `NeedsTempColor() { return false; }`, so no intermediate
+  colour target is inserted.
+* `Common/RenderDisplayContext.h:98`
+  `bool IsHighDynamicRangeDisplay() const { return false; /* CRendererCVars::CV_r_HDRSwapChain */ }`
+  — hard-coded false. `Common/Renderer.h:1309` `IsHDRDisplayEnabled()` is therefore always false,
+  and `CD3D9Renderer::ResolveHighDynamicRangeDisplay` (`XRenderD3D9/DriverD3D.cpp:1326`)
+  early-returns at `:1329`.
+* `SetColorSpace1` / `CheckColorSpaceSupport` exist **only** as COM passthroughs in the DX12
+  emulation shim — `XRenderD3D9/DX12/GI/CCryDX12SwapChain.hpp:269-284`,
+  `XRenderD3D9/DX12/GI/CCryDX12GIOutput.cpp:59-61`. No `DXGI_COLOR_SPACE_RGB_*` constant is
+  passed anywhere in `Code/`; there is no `IDXGIOutput6` / `DXGI_OUTPUT_DESC1` capability query.
+* Vulkan is hard-coded SDR — `XRenderD3D9/Vulkan/API/VKSwapChain.cpp:146`
+  `Info.imageColorSpace = VK_COLORSPACE_SRGB_NONLINEAR_KHR;`.
+
