+## B. Clamps and thresholds between lighting and the tone-mapper
+
+### B3. Every clamp / threshold / limited-range encode on the colour path
+
+**Deferred lighting output is clean.** The tiled shading compute shader writes the unclamped sum:
+
+* `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/TiledShading.cfi:1054`
+  `float3 finalCol = diffuseAcc * surfAlbedo + specularAcc;`
+* `TiledShading.cfi:1071` `HDRSceneTargetUAV[pixelCoord] = float3( finalCol );`
+
+There is **no `saturate` on the lighting result**. The nearby `saturate` at `TiledShading.cfi:1052`
+is a diffuse/specular energy-conservation term on the albedo — a weight, not a range limit.
+
+Everything after that, in pipeline order
+(`CStandardGraphicsPipeline::ExecuteHDRPostProcessing()`,
+`XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:169-267`):
+
+| # | Where | file:line | What it does | Affects |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `$HDRTarget → $HDRTargetPrev` copy | `StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:188` | `CStretchRectPass` into an **R11G11B10F** target (`Common/UtilityPasses.cpp:24-60`) | **colour** — negatives clipped, precision lost; read by SSR / water / motion blur |
+| 2 | DOF layer downscale / gather | `DepthOfField.cpp:704-706`, `:801-803`, `:901-903` | targets are `nHDRAFormat` = fp16 | colour, no clamp |
+| 3 | DOF composition alpha | `DepthOfField.cfx:1614`, `:1633` `saturate(cLayerNear.a)` | blend weight | **mask/weight only** |
+| 4 | DOF gather normalisation | `DepthOfField.cfx:1552-1553` `max(caccNear, 1e-6)` | divisor guard | weight |
+| 5 | Motion-blur source copy | `MotionBlur.cpp:185` `m_passCopy.Execute(m_pTexHDRTarget, m_pTexSceneTargetR11G11B10F[0])` | **R11G11B10F** | **colour** |
+| 6 | Motion-blur input select | `MotionBlur.cpp:201` — `m_pTexSceneTargetR11G11B10F[0]` or `m_pTexHDRTargetPrev[]` | both R11G11B10F | **colour** |
+| 7 | Motion-blur weights | `MotionBlur.cfx:45-46`, `:158`, `:164` `saturate(...)` | sample weights / velocity | **weight only** |
+| 8 | Half/quarter HDR downsample (bloom + exposure feed) | `StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:208-223` → `CStableDownsamplePass::Execute` (`Common/UtilityPasses.cpp:427-450`) | technique `DownsampleStable` | colour |
+| 9 | Firefly suppression inside that downsample | `PostEffects.cfx:305-353` `tex /= 1 + GetLuminance(tex)` per tap; inverse `block /= (1 - GetLuminance(block))` at `:356-364` | reversible Reinhard weighting, but exact only for the average; enabled when `r_HDRBloomQuality >= 1` (default 2, `Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1212-1213`) | **colour of the bloom / exposure feed** |
+| 10 | Luminance measure — NaN filter | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:750` `all(isfinite(cTex)) ? GetLuminance(cTex) : 0` | drops non-finite | metering |
+| 11 | Luminance measure — albedo floor | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:743` `max(..., 0.01)`; `:747` `baseColorLum = 0.2` for zero-albedo (sky) | metering |
+| 12 | Luminance measure — log epsilon | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:752-753` `log(fLum + 1e-6)` | metering |
+| 13 | Eye-adaptation accumulate | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:792` `max(0, vAdaptedLum + …)` | metering (clamps negative luminance) |
+| 14 | Streak / sunstar threshold | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:168-181`, soft-knee high pass on `max(r,g,b)`; threshold `HDR_Streaks_Threshold` default **4.0** (`Common/PostProcess/PostEffects.h:412`) | **colour of the streak layer only**; source untouched |
+| 15 | Sun-shafts mask | `Sunshafts.cfx:136-151` writes `sceneDepth * dot(sceneCol, 1.32)` into `m_pTexDisplayTargetScaled[]` = **R10G10B10A2 UNORM** (`GraphicsPipeline.cpp:289-291`, `SunShafts.cpp:36-43`) | **colour, hard `[0,1]` clamp** |
+| 16 | Sun-shafts gen falloff | `Sunshafts.cfx:166` `saturate(fSign) * saturate(1 - saturate(length(...)))` | radial weight | weight |
+| 17 | **Tone map — exposure clamp** | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:810` `EV100 = clamp(EV100, HDREyeAdaptation.x, HDREyeAdaptation.y)` (EV mode); `:827` `fExposure = clamp(fSceneKey/vAdaptedLum.x, HDREyeAdaptation.y, HDREyeAdaptation.z)` (legacy mode) | **exposure scalar** |
+| 18 | **Tone map — negative clip** | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:838` `half4 c = half4(max(cColor, 0), HDRFilmCurve.w)` | **colour** — negatives clipped |
+| 19 | **Tone map — output saturate** | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:841` `cScene = saturate(compressedCol / compressedCol.w)` | **colour → `[0,1]`** |
+| 20 | **Tone map — sRGB encode** | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:844` exact sRGB piecewise curve | **colour → display-referred** |
+| 21 | Second saturate on the way out | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:871` `return saturate(vSample)` in `HDRToneMapSample` | colour (redundant) |
+| 22 | Sun-shaft composite | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:964` `oSample += shafts * SunShafts_SunCol * (1 - oSample)` | **display-referred additive**, already past the sRGB encode |
+| 23 | Colour-chart LUT | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:968` → `PostEffectsLib.cfi:191` `float3 lookup = saturate(cImage) * scale + bias` | **colour, `[0,1]` domain only** |
+| 24 | HDR dithering | `HDRPostProcess.cfx:970` (`%_RT_SAMPLE6`) → `ApplyRandomDithering` `:879-885`, ±1/255 in sRGB space; `r_HDRDithering` default **1** (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:2918-2922`) | colour, ±1 LSB |
+| 25 | Tone-map render target | `ToneMapping.cpp:96` `SetRenderTarget(0, m_pTexDisplayTargetDst)` → **R10G10B10A2 UNORM** | **colour, hard clamp** |
+| 26 | TAA history neighbourhood clamp | `PostAA.cfx:255` `cHistory.rgb = clamp(cHistory.rgb, cMin, cMax)` | colour (intended AA behaviour) |
+| 27 | TAA sharpen | `PostAA.cfx:179` `cM = saturate(lerp(cBlur, cM, params.x))` | **colour → `[0,1]`** |
+| 28 | PostAA composite sharpening | `PostAA.cfx:1037` `sqrt(saturate(lerp(cFiltered, Color*Color, vParams.x)))` | **colour → `[0,1]`**, in a squared ("gamma 2") space |
+| 29 | PostAA composite output | `PostAA.cfx:1064`, `:1185` `OUT.Color = saturate(OUT.Color)` | colour |
+| 30 | Optional broadcast range limit | `PostAA.cfx:1188-1191` `LimitREC709_8Bit()` (`CommonMath.cfi:231-235`, 16–235) behind `r_ColorRangeCompression` (default **0**, `Common/RendererCVars.cpp:2207-2211`) | colour, off by default |
+
+C++ constants worth naming:
+
+* `RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE = 10000.0f` — `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IRenderer.h:778`, with the
+  comment at `:777` `//! Scale factor between photometric and internal light units.`
+  Mirrored in HLSL as `#define LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE 10000.0f` at `HDRPostProcess.cfx:799`.
+* `m_vHDREyeAdaptation = Vec3(0.05f, 0.8f, 0.9f)` — `Cry3DEngine/3dEngine.cpp:239` (overwritten
+  every frame by TOD, see §C5).
+* `m_vHDRFilmCurveParams = Vec4(1,1,1,1)` — `Cry3DEngine/3dEngine.cpp:238`.
+* `m_fHDRBloomAmount = 0.0f` — `Cry3DEngine/3dEngine.cpp:240`; scaled ×0.3 at
+  `Cry3DEngine/3dEngine.cpp:2755` and again ×1/8 at `ToneMapping.cpp:131`.
+* **`r_HDRRangeAdapt` is dead code.** `#define HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_DEFAULT_VAL 0` at
+  `Common/Renderer.h:118`; the cvar and its `Max` / `MaxRange` / `LBufferMax` siblings
+  (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1260-1283`) have **no readers anywhere in the renderer**.
+* **No bloom threshold exists.** `HDRBloomGaussianPS` (`HDRPostProcess.cfx:126-149`) is a pure
+  separable Gaussian over the whole quarter-res HDR target. The only thresholding in the glare
+  family is the streak / diffraction / halation soft knee (row 14).
+* `r_HDRVignetteAmount` default **0.0** — `Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1543`; the vignetting map is
+  `%ENGINE%/EngineAssets/Shading/vignetting.tif` (`Common/RendererResources.cpp:289`).
+
+### B4. Where TAA / PostAA sits, and what range it assumes
+
+**PostAA runs entirely *after* tone-mapping**, on display-referred sRGB data.
+
+* `CStandardGraphicsPipeline::Execute()` calls `ExecuteHDRPostProcessing()` (which ends with the
+  tone-map) at `StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:472`, then the LDR post stage at `:486-489`.
+* `CPostAAStage::Execute()` (`PostAA.cpp:545-585`) takes `pCurrRT = m_pTexDisplayTargetDst`,
+  `pTempRT = m_pTexDisplayTargetSrc` (`:552-553`) — both R10G10B10A2 UNORM — and writes the final
+  composite into `RenderView()->GetColorTarget()` (`:572`), the R8G8B8A8 output.
+* The post-effect dispatcher switches off the "alt back buffer" exactly at the PostAA slot:
+  `if (id >= EPostEffectID::PostAA) m_context.EnableAltBackBuffer(false);` in
+  `CPostEffectStage::Execute()` (`XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/PostEffects.cpp`).
+
+Resolve details:
+
+* **SMAA edge detection is luminance-weighted and assumes sRGB-encoded input.**
+  `PostAA.cfx:329` `const half3 weights = GetLuminanceWeights();` then `:330-332`, `:344-345`,
+  `:352-353` `SRGBToLinearApproximation(LumEdSMAA_Source.Load(...), weights)`.
+  `GetLuminanceWeights()` returns Rec.709 `(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722)` — `CommonMath.cfi:128-131`.
+* **The temporal resolve is a plain RGB neighbourhood clamp, not a tone-mapped resolve.**
+  `PostAA.cfx:255` `cHistory.rgb = clamp(cHistory.rgb, cMin, cMax);` with `cMin/cMax` from the
+  3×3 neighbourhood; TSAA weights on `length()` differences (`:225-242`). There is **no**
+  `x/(1+L)` tone-map / inverse-tone-map pair anywhere in `PostAA.cfx`.
+* Assumed range is therefore **`[0,1]` display-referred**: the history buffer is UNORM
+  (`PostAA.cpp:627`), the sharpen filter does `sqrt(saturate(...))` on squared values
+  (`PostAA.cfx:1037`), and the composite ends in `saturate` (`:1185`).
+
+Default AA mode is `eAT_DEFAULT_AA = eAT_SMAA_1TX` (`Common/Renderer.h:30`, registered
+`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1452`), which *is* in `eAT_REQUIRES_PREVIOUSFRAME_MASK`
+(`Common/Renderer.h:40`) — so the temporal path with the UNORM history buffer is the default.
+
+---
+
+## C. Exposure and tone-mapping
+
+### C5. Eye adaptation, end to end
+
+**Pass 1 — initial luminance downsample.** `CAutoExposureStage::MeasureLuminance()` —
+`XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/AutoExposure.cpp:28-127`. Technique `HDRSampleLumInitial`
+(`:57`), rendering into `s_ptexHDRToneMaps[NUM_HDR_TONEMAP_TEXTURES-1]` (`:61`). Inputs (`:65-68`):
+`m_pTexHDRTargetScaled[1][0]` (quarter-res HDR) plus the three G-buffer targets.
+
+Shader `HDRSampleLumInitialPS` — `HDRPostProcess.cfx:725-757`. Four rotated-grid taps
+(offsets set at `AutoExposure.cpp:81-82`); per tap it decodes the G-buffer for an albedo estimate
+(`HDRPostProcess.cfx:736-747`) and accumulates two log quantities:
+
+```hlsl
+vLumInfo.x += log(fLum + 1e-6);                      // Luminance     // :752
+vLumInfo.y += log(fLum / baseColorLum * PI + 1e-6);  // Illuminance   // :753
+```
+
+**Pass 2 — iterative 4×4 reduction.** `AutoExposure.cpp:91-121`, technique
+`HDRSampleLumIterative` (`:103`), shader `HDRPostProcess.cfx:761-778`. The last iteration
+(`curTexture == 0` → `%_RT_SAMPLE0`, set at `AutoExposure.cpp:98-99`) applies
+`vResampleSum = exp(vResampleSum)` (`HDRPostProcess.cfx:773`), turning the log-average into a
+geometric mean. Result lands in the 1×1 `s_ptexHDRToneMaps[0]`, copied to
+`m_pTexHDRMeasuredLuminance[gpu]` at `AutoExposure.cpp:123-126`.
+
+**Pass 3 — temporal adaptation.** `CAutoExposureStage::AdjustExposure()` —
+`AutoExposure.cpp:129-173`. Ping-pongs the eight 1×1 `s_ptexHDRAdaptedLuminanceCur[]` textures
+(`:136-142`), technique `HDRCalculateAdaptedLum` (`:149`), shader `HDRPostProcess.cfx:786-793`:
+
+```hlsl
+return max(0, vAdaptedLum + (vCurrentLum - vAdaptedLum) * ElapsedTime.yyzz);   // :792
+```
+
+with `ElapsedTime.y = 1 - exp(-r_HDREyeAdaptationSpeed * dt)` and
+`.z = 1 - exp(-r_HDRRangeAdaptationSpeed * dt)` (`AutoExposure.cpp:164-169`). Defaults:
+`r_HDREyeAdaptationSpeed` **1.0** (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1286-1288`),
+`r_HDRRangeAdaptationSpeed` **4.0** (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1294-1296`). The result texture
+pointer is published as `CRendererResources::s_ptexCurLumTexture` (`AutoExposure.cpp:142`).
+
+**The two modes.** `r_HDREyeAdaptationMode` is registered at
+`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1290-1293` with **default 2**:
+
+```
+  1: Standard auto exposure (using EV values)
+  2: Legacy auto exposure for backwards compatibility (CE 3.6 to 3.8.1)
+```
+
+`CToneMappingStage::Execute()` maps that onto a shader flag and a constant:
+
+```cpp
+if (CRenderer::CV_r_HDREyeAdaptationMode == 2) rtMask |= g_HWSR_MaskBit[HWSR_SAMPLE4]; // ToneMapping.cpp:80-81
+m_passToneMapping.SetConstant(eyeAdaptationName,
+    CRenderer::CV_r_HDREyeAdaptationMode == 2 ? hdrSetupParams[4] : hdrSetupParams[3],
+    eHWSC_Pixel);                                                                      // ToneMapping.cpp:126
+```
+
+Mode 1 — **EV-based**, `ComputeExposure()` at `HDRPostProcess.cfx:801-816`:
+
+```hlsl
+half EV100 = log2(fIlluminance * LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE * 100.0 / 330.0);                       // :804
+EV100 -= ((clamp(log10(fIlluminance*LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE + 1), 0.1, 5.2) - 3.0)/2.0)
+         * HDREyeAdaptation.z;                                                           // :807
+EV100 = clamp(EV100, HDREyeAdaptation.x, HDREyeAdaptation.y);                            // :810
+float maxLum = exp2(EV100);                                                              // :813
+return (LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE / 1.2f) * rcp(maxLum);                                           // :815
+```
+
+This is a textbook ISO-100 photographic model: `C = 330`, `L_sat = 1.2 · 2^EV100`. Here
+`HDREyeAdaptation = hdrSetupParams[3] = Vec4(m_vHDREyeAdaptation, 1)` = (EV min, EV max, EV auto
+compensation). TOD defaults, `Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp`:
+
+* `:379` "EV Min" `PARAM_HDR_EYEADAPTATION_EV_MIN` default **4.5** (range −10…20)
+* `:380` "EV Max" `PARAM_HDR_EYEADAPTATION_EV_MAX` default **17.0**
+* `:381` "EV Auto compensation" default **1.5** (range −5…5)
+
+pushed into the 3D engine at `Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:1016-1019`. That is a **12.5-stop
+adaptation window** before auto-compensation.
+
+Mode 2 — **legacy Krawczyk**, `HDRPostProcess.cfx:824-828` under `%_RT_SAMPLE4`:
+
+```hlsl
+const half fSceneKey = 1.03h - 2.0h / (2.0h + log2(vAdaptedLum.x + 1.0));                // :826
+fExposure = clamp(fSceneKey / vAdaptedLum.x, HDREyeAdaptation.y, HDREyeAdaptation.z);    // :827
+```
+
+with `HDREyeAdaptation = hdrSetupParams[4] = Vec4(m_vHDREyeAdaptationLegacy, 1)` = (scene key,
+min exposure, max exposure). TOD defaults, shown under the "Obsolete" group,
+`Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:426-428`: scene key **0.18**, min exposure **0.36**, max
+exposure **2.8** (`Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:1021-1024`).
+
+**How the exposure scalar reaches the shader.** It does not — the shader *computes* it from the
+1×1 adapted-luminance texture:
+
+* Texture slot 1 = `CRendererResources::s_ptexCurLumTexture` — `ToneMapping.cpp:105`.
+* Constant `HDREyeAdaptation` (`float4`, declared `HDRPostProcess.cfx:26`) — set at
+  `ToneMapping.cpp:126`.
+* Read in the shader as `luminanceTex.Load(int3(0,0,0))` → `vAdaptedLum`
+  (`HDRPostProcess.cfx:958`); `.x` is average luminance, `.y` average illuminance.
+* `FilmMapping()` calls `ComputeExposure(vAdaptedLum.y)` at `HDRPostProcess.cfx:820`.
+
+**Every consumer of the exposure / luminance data:**
+
+| Consumer | file:line | What it reads |
+|---|---|---|
+| `CToneMappingStage` (main) | `ToneMapping.cpp:105`, `:126` | `s_ptexCurLumTexture`, `HDREyeAdaptation` |
+| `CToneMappingStage::ExecuteDebug` | `ToneMapping.cpp:179`, `:193` | same (`r_HDRDebug 2` = `HDRPostProcess.cfx:982-986`, exposure ×1e-5 then sRGB, no film curve) |
+| `CToneMappingStage::DisplayDebugInfo` | `ToneMapping.cpp:239-291` | CPU readback of `s_ptexHDRToneMaps[0]`; replicates both exposure formulas for the on-screen text |
+| **`CPostAAStage::DoFinalComposition` (film grain)** | `PostAA.cpp:462`, `:476`, `:495` | binds `s_ptexCurLumTexture` to slot 7 and `hdrSetupParams[4]` to `HDREyeAdaptation`; used by `ApplyFilmGrain` (`PostAA.cfx:905-923`) **only** when `r_GrainEnableExposureThreshold` (default **0**, `Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1302-1305`) |
+| **`CScreenSpaceReflectionsStage`** | `ScreenSpaceReflections.cpp:63` | binds `m_pTexHDRMeasuredLuminance[gpu]` to the raytracing pass |
+| `CFogStage` | `Fog.cpp:236-239` | `m_vSceneLuminanceInfo.x` and `m_fAdaptedSceneScale` — **both hard-wired to 1.0**, see §C7 |
+
+Bloom, DOF, sun shafts and motion blur do **not** read exposure.
+
+**Note for the CinematicCamera plugin.** `CCinematicCameraComponent::ApplyExposureGlobalParam()`
+(`Code/CryPlugins/CinematicCamera/Module/CinematicCameraComponent.cpp:1691-1769`) drives
+`E3DPARAM_HDR_EYEADAPTATION_PARAMS`, i.e. `hdrSetupParams[3]` — the **EV-based** window
+(`:1742-1744` AutoBiased, `:1759-1760` Manual). With the shipped default
+`r_HDREyeAdaptationMode = 2` the tone-mapper feeds `hdrSetupParams[4]` instead
+(`ToneMapping.cpp:126`) and takes the legacy Krawczyk branch (`HDRPostProcess.cfx:826-827`), so
+those writes have **no effect** unless `r_HDREyeAdaptationMode 1` is set.
+
+### C6. The tone-map itself
+
+* Stage: `CToneMappingStage::Execute()` — `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/ToneMapping.cpp:44-148`.
+* Shader: `CShaderMan::s_shHDRPostProcess` (`ToneMapping.cpp:59`), technique **`HDRFinalPass`**
+  (`ToneMapping.cpp:94`), declared `HDRPostProcess.cfx:1750-1757`, pixel shader
+  `HDRFinalScenePS` (`HDRPostProcess.cfx:920-976`).
+* Siblings: `HDRFinalDebugPass` (`:1759-1766`, C++ `ToneMapping.cpp:150-200`) and
+  `HDRFinalPassFixedExposure` (`:1768-1775`) — the latter's C++ entry
+  `CToneMappingStage::ExecuteFixedExposure` is **`return;`-ed out** at `ToneMapping.cpp:206-207`,
+  so it is dead.
+* Static feature flags (`ToneMapping.cpp:78-91`): `SAMPLE1` colour grading, `SAMPLE2` vignetting,
+  `SAMPLE3` bloom, `SAMPLE4` legacy exposure, `SAMPLE5` sun shafts, `SAMPLE6` dithering.
+
+**The curve** — `FilmMapping()`, `HDRPostProcess.cfx:818-846`, the Hable/Uncharted-2 filmic
+operator with its shoulder/linear/toe knobs scaled by `HDRFilmCurve`:
+
+```hlsl
+half3 cColor = fVignetting * fExposure * lerp(cScene, cBloom, saturate(HDRBloomColor));   // :830
+half fLuminance = GetLuminance(cColor);                                                   // :833
+cColor = fLuminance + HDRColorBalance.a * (cColor - fLuminance);   // saturation          // :834
+cColor *= HDRColorBalance.rgb;                                     // colour balance      // :835
+half4 c = half4(max(cColor, 0), HDRFilmCurve.w);                                          // :838
+const half ShoStren = 0.22*HDRFilmCurve.x, LinStren = 0.3*HDRFilmCurve.y, LinAngle = 0.1,
+           ToeStren = 0.2, ToeNum = 0.01*HDRFilmCurve.z, ToeDenom = 0.3;                  // :839
+half4 compressedCol = ((c*(ShoStren*c + LinAngle*LinStren) + ToeStren*ToeNum)
+                     / (c*(ShoStren*c + LinStren)     + ToeStren*ToeDenom)) - ToeNum/ToeDenom; // :840
+cScene = saturate(compressedCol / compressedCol.w);                                       // :841
+cScene = (cScene < 0.0031308) ? 12.92h*cScene
+       : 1.055h*pow(cScene, 1.0h/2.4h) - half3(0.055h,0.055h,0.055h);                     // :844
+```
+
+`HDRFilmCurve` = `hdrSetupParams[0]` = `m_vHDRFilmCurveParams` (`Cry3DEngine/3dEngine.cpp:2754`),
+default `(1,1,1,1)` (`Cry3DEngine/3dEngine.cpp:238`) → shoulder 0.22, linear 0.3, toe-numerator
+0.01, white point 1.0 (`.w` is the `compressedCol.w` normaliser).
+
+There is **no separate "HDR_Legacy" curve branch** — the `%_RT_SAMPLE4` branch swaps the
+*exposure* formula only.
+
+**Gamma / sRGB encode point:** `HDRPostProcess.cfx:844`, inside `FilmMapping`, using the exact
+piecewise sRGB inverse-EOTF. That is the only encode in the main path; duplicate inlined copies
+exist at `HDRPostProcess.cfx:986` (debug pass), `:1021` (dead fixed-exposure pass),
+`DeferredShading.cfx:1090-1093` (`ToSRGB` for the G-buffer debug view) and `ReferenceImage.cfx:31`.
+Everything downstream — sun shafts (`:964`), colour chart (`:968`), dithering (`:970`), PostAA,
+film grain, sharpening, vignette/viewfinder overlays — operates on **sRGB-encoded,
+display-referred** values.
+
+**Colour grading relative to the tone-map:** applied **after** the curve *and* after the sRGB
+encode, at `HDRPostProcess.cfx:966-969` (`%_RT_SAMPLE1` → `TexColorChart2D(...)`), with
+`%_RT_SAMPLE1` set at `ToneMapping.cpp:82-83` and the chart bound to slot 8 at `:108`.
+
+* LUT resolution: `IColorGradingCtrl::s_colorChartSize = 16`, unwrapped to a **256 × 16** 2-D
+  strip — `CryCommon/Cry3DEngine/IColorGradingCtrl.h:22-24`.
+* LUT format: `const ETEX_Format COLORCHART_FORMAT = eTF_R8G8B8A8;` —
+  `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/ColorGrading.cpp:9`; targets `ColorGradingMergedLayer`
+  (`:38`) and `ColorGradingFinalMerged` (`:44`). The RC preset treats charts as raw data —
+  `Code/Tools/RC/rc.ini:348-354` `[ColorChart] colorspace=linear,linear`.
+* Lookup: `PostEffectsLib.cfi:183-208`, with `float3 lookup = saturate(cImage) * scale + bias;`
+  at `:191` — **domain hard-limited to `[0,1]`** — hardware bilinear within a slice and a manual
+  lerp across the two neighbouring blue slices (`:201-206`).
+* Chart build is two passes: `MergeColorCharts` (`PostEffectsGame.cfx:1169-1201`, dispatched
+  `ColorGrading.cpp:145-176`) then `CombineColorGradingWithColorChart`
+  (`PostEffectsGame.cfx:1237-1282`, dispatched `ColorGrading.cpp:185-218`), which bakes levels
+  (`:1014`), photo filter (`:1030`), the composed colour matrix (`:1049`) and selective colour
+  (`:1082`) into the chart. Cached every `r_ColorgradingChartsCache` frames
+  (`ColorGrading.cpp:240`).
+* A second application exists on the lens-flare path: `PostAA.cfx:1053-1055` (`%_RT_SAMPLE5`),
+  enabled from `PostAA.cpp:430-439` (`r_FlaresEnableColorGrading`).
+
+### C7. Existing pre-exposure, and where one could go
+
+**There is no pre-exposure today, but the hook already exists and is wired.**
+
+`CD3D9Renderer::m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` (declared `XRenderD3D9/DriverD3D.h:699`, alongside
+`m_fAdaptedSceneScale` `:698`, `m_fScotopicSceneScale` `:697`, `m_vSceneLuminanceInfo` `:695`) is
+multiplied into light colours **at injection time**:
+
+* `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/TiledLightVolumes.cpp:824-828`
+  `float intensityScale = rd->m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer;` then
+  `lightShadeInfo.color = Vec4(renderLight.m_Color.r * intensityScale, …)` — **every
+  deferred/tiled light**.
+* `Common/RenderView.cpp:591` and `:599`
+  `sunColor *= gcpRendD3D->m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer;  // Apply LBuffers range rescale` —
+  **the sun**, in both the secondary-viewport and main-viewport branches.
+* `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/ClipVolumes.cpp:272`
+  `Vec4(gEnv->p3DEngine->GetSkyColor() * gcpRendD3D->m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer, …)` — **sky /
+  clip-volume ambient**.
+* `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/VolumetricFog.cpp:1043`
+  `const float itensityScale = rd->m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer;` — **volumetric fog lights**.
+* `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/Fog.cpp:236-239` passes
+  `Vec4(m_vSceneLuminanceInfo.x, m_fAdaptedSceneScale, 0, 0)` to the fog shader as `HDRParams`.
+
+Every assignment to these variables in the tree sets them to **1.0** and nothing else:
+`Common/RendererResources.cpp:593`, `XRenderD3D9/D3DHDRRender.cpp:219`,
+`XRenderD3D9/D3DRendPipeline.cpp:607`, `XRenderD3D9/DriverD3D.cpp:78` and `:127`. The mechanism
+is a live but permanently-neutral pre-exposure multiplier.
+
+Of the four siblings, **only `m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` is actually wired into shading** (the
+five sites above). `m_fAdaptedSceneScale` has exactly one reader, `Fog.cpp:237`, which feeds the
+dead `HDRParams2` constant (§G14); `m_vSceneLuminanceInfo` likewise has one reader, `Fog.cpp:236`,
+into the same dead constant; and **`m_fScotopicSceneScale` has no readers at all**
+(declared `XRenderD3D9/DriverD3D.h:697`, assigned only in the five initialisers above).
+
+The **earliest point** at which exposure could be applied is therefore exactly those five sites,
+before any light is written into `m_pTexHDRTarget`. The **next-earliest** single choke point is
+the tiled-shading write itself (`TiledShading.cfi:1071`); after that, the
+`$HDRTarget → $HDRTargetPrev` copy at `StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:188`.
+
+Note that pre-exposure at those sites would **not** cover emissive materials, which bypass the
+deferred path entirely (see §D4), nor the skybox (§D3), nor anything drawn into the forward
+transparent lists.
+
+Other "scene scale" constants:
+
+* `RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE = 10000.0f` — `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IRenderer.h:778`. See §D.
+* `C3DEngine::m_fLightsHDRDynamicPowerFactor` — `Cry3DEngine/3dEngine.cpp:236`, init `0.0f`.
+* `C3DEngine::m_fHDRMultiplier` = `powf(HDRDynamicMultiplier, PARAM_HDR_DYNAMIC_POWER_FACTOR)`
+  — `Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:1014`, with `HDRDynamicMultiplier = 2.0f`
+  (`CryCommon/Cry3DEngine/I3DEngine.h:43`) and the TOD default power factor **0.0** under the
+  "Deprecated" group (`Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:417`) ⇒ **1.0**, a no-op. It still gates
+  the fog and night-sky multipliers (`Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:1057-1064`).
+* **`r_HDRGammaMultiplier` does not exist** in this tree. The only gamma cvar path is the OS
+  gamma ramp, `r_Gamma` (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:2850-2854`, default 1.0), applied outside the
+  render graph via `SetDeviceGammaRamp` (`XRenderD3D9/D3DSystem.cpp:468`, ramp built at
+  `:477-529`, entry point `SetGammaDelta` at `:531`, driven per-frame from
+  `XRenderD3D9/DriverD3D.cpp:1085-1086`).
+
+### C8. Ordered list of passes after the tone-map (the "LDR" stage)
