+## D. Units and scale of light sources
+
+### D9a. Point / projector / area / probe lights — **no physical unit at all**
+
+Authored properties, `Code/CryPlugins/CryDefaultEntities/Module/DefaultComponents/Lights/ILightComponent.h`:
+
+* `:74-76` `ColorF m_color = ColorF(1.f); Schematyc::Range<0,10000,0,100> m_diffuseMultiplier = 1.f;
+  Schematyc::Range<0,10000> m_specularMultiplier = 1.f;`
+* Reflected at `:182-183` with the labels `"Diffuse Multiplier"` / `"Specular Multiplier"` —
+  **no unit string, default 1.0**.
+* `:58` `Schematyc::Range<0,64000> m_attenuationBulbSize = SRenderLight().m_fAttenuationBulbSize;`
+  (default **0.1 m**, `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IShader.h:2462`), described at `:158`
+  `"…a value of 1 means that the light is at full intensity within a 1 meter ball before it
+  begins to fall-off."`
+* Area shape `:114-115` `m_width = 1.0f; m_height = 1.0f;` — **area size never normalises
+  intensity anywhere**, so doubling the plate doubles emitted flux.
+* `PointLightComponent.h:63`, `:75` — `m_radius` default `10.f`.
+
+Component → `SRenderLight`, `PointLightComponent.cpp`:
+
+```cpp
+light.SetLightColor(m_color.m_color * m_color.m_diffuseMultiplier);   // :43
+light.SetSpecularMult(m_color.m_specularMultiplier);                  // :44
+light.m_fHDRDynamic = 0.f;                                            // :52
+```
+
+Identical in `ProjectorLightComponent.cpp:45-48` and `EnvironmentProbeComponent.h:407-410`. It is
+a plain component-wise multiply — **no conversion**.
+
+`m_fHDRDynamic` is dead: `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IShader.h:2411`
+`float m_fHDRDynamic = 0; //!< <DEPRECATED> …`, and its only renderer consumer is commented out at
+`Common/Renderer.cpp:2015-2020`.
+
+Radius is *derived from* intensity — `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IShader.h:2133-2145`:
+
+```cpp
+float fIntensity = m_Color.Luminance() * GetIntensityScale();
+m_fRadius = min(GetRadiationRadius(fIntensity, IlluminanceThreshold()), m_fClipRadius);
+...
+// Adjust light intensity so that the intended brightness is reached 1 meter from the light's surface
+return sqr(1.0f + m_fAttenuationBulbSize);
+```
+
+with `#define ILLUMINANCE_THRESHOLD 0.004f` (`IShader.h:2063`, cvar
+`e_LightIlluminanceThreshold` at `Cry3DEngine/cvars.cpp:888-889`) and
+`GetRadiationRadius` at `IShader.h:2072-2077`. A sanity clamp at `IShader.h:2167` rejects any
+channel > 1000.0f.
+
+The renderer then re-applies the bulb normalisation — `TiledLightVolumes.cpp:895-903`:
+
+```cpp
+// Adjust light intensity so that the intended brightness is reached 1 meter from the light's surface
+// Solve I * 1 / (1 + d/lightsize)^2 = 1
+float intensityMul = 1.0f + 1.0f / lightShadeInfo.attenuationParams.x;
+intensityMul *= intensityMul;
+lightShadeInfo.color.x *= intensityMul;   // .y, .z likewise
+```
+
+(guarded by `if (!ambientLight)` at `:893`). With the default bulb 0.1 m, `intensityMul = 121`;
+the shader divides it back out in `GetPhysicalLightAttenuation`
+(`Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/shadeLib.cfi:193-207`). Accumulation at
+`TiledShading.cfi:1030-1034`; the forward path names the quantity explicitly at
+`TiledShading.cfi:267` `lightParams.illuminance = Fwd_TiledLightsShadeInfo[…].color.rgb;`.
+
+There is **no 1/π in the diffuse BRDF** (`shadeLib.cfi:857-880`).
+
+**Is there any candela / lumen / watt conversion for these lights? No.** Sweeps for `candela`,
+`lumen`, `lux`, `nit`, `cd/m`, `kcd`, `photometric`, `Watt`, `radiance`, `irradiance` across
+`Code/`, `Engine/` and `Editor/` return, in the lighting domain, only:
+
+| Hit | file:line |
+|---|---|
+| `//! Scale factor between photometric and internal light units.` | `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IRenderer.h:777` |
+| `ColorF m_Emittance;  //!< RGB: Color, Alpha: Intensity (kcd/m2 or kilonits).` | `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IShader.h:407` |
+| `"Sun intensity (lux)"` / `"Intensity (lux)"` | `Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:258`, `:312` |
+| `"Emissive Intensity (kcd/m2)"` | `Code/Sandbox/EditorQt/Material/MaterialDialog.cpp:449`; `Code/Sandbox/Plugins/MaterialEditorPlugin/MaterialProperties.cpp:322`, `:335` |
+| `"Emissive (kcd/m2)"` (particles) | `Cry3DEngine/ParticleSystem/Features/FeatureAppearance.cpp:351` |
+| `"Specifies how much luminance (kcd/m2) the fog emits."` | `CryDefaultEntities/Module/DefaultComponents/Effects/FogComponent.h:58` |
+| `Average Luminance (cd/m2)` debug HUD | `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/ToneMapping.cpp:264` |
+
+Local lights are the one authored light type with **no photometric unit whatever**.
