+### D9b. The sun
+
+**`e_SunIntensity` does not exist in 5.7.1** — grep across the tree returns nothing.
+(`e_Sun`, `Cry3DEngine/cvars.cpp:563`, is a boolean.) Sun intensity is a Time-of-Day variable:
+
+`Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:257-259`:
+
+```cpp
+AddVar("Sun", "", "Sun color", PARAM_SUN_COLOR, TYPE_COLOR, 255/255, 248/255, 248/255);   // :257
+AddVar("Sun", "Sun intensity (lux)", "Sun intensity", PARAM_SUN_INTENSITY, TYPE_FLOAT,
+       119000.0f, 0.0f, 550000.0f);                                                       // :258
+AddVar("Sun", "", "Sun specular multiplier", PARAM_SUN_SPECULAR_MULTIPLIER, TYPE_FLOAT,
+       1.0f, 0.0f, 4.0f);                                                                 // :259
+```
+
+(For `TYPE_FLOAT` the three trailing values are default/min/max; signature
+`Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.h:124`, impl `EnvironmentPreset.cpp:556-560`.)
+**Shipped defaults: 119 000 lux, colour (1.000, 0.9725, 0.9725), spec mult 1.0.**
+
+lux → engine units, `Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:463-474`:
+
+```cpp
+Vec3 ConvertIlluminanceToLightColor(float illuminance, Vec3 colorRGB)
+{
+	illuminance /= RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE;
+	ColorF color(colorRGB);
+	color.adjust_luminance(illuminance);
+	// Divide by PI as this is not done in the BRDF at the moment
+	Vec3 finalColor = color.toVec3() / gf_PI;
+	return finalColor;
+}
+```
+
+(`adjust_luminance` uses `(0.212671, 0.715160, 0.072169)` — `CryCommon/CryMath/Cry_Color.h:1046`,
+comment: *"Color and luminance are expected to be linear."*)
+
+Applied at `Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:1175-1177`:
+
+```cpp
+const float sunIntensityLux(GetValue(PARAM_SUN_INTENSITY).x * sunMultiplier);
+const Vec3 sunEmission(ConvertIlluminanceToLightColor(sunIntensityLux, sunColor));
+p3DEngine->SetSunColor(sunEmission);
+```
+
+`sunMultiplier` is the dawn/dusk fade only (`TimeOfDay.cpp:1052`, `:1127-1162`), 1.0 at midday.
+Storage `Cry3DEngine/3dEngine.cpp:1483-1490`; read back `:1758-1761`.
+
+**Default sun in engine units: 119 000 / 10 000 / π = 3.788.**
+
+Sun → render light → GPU: `Cry3DEngine/LightEntity.cpp:155-160` (`DLF_DIRECTIONAL | DLF_SUN`,
+radius 1e8, `SetLightColor(GetSunColor())`); `Common/RenderView.cpp:583-603` (`GetSunLightColor`,
+with the `m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` multiply at `:591`/`:599`); injected as an ordinary tile
+light at `TiledLightVolumes.cpp:742-746` with
+`attenuationParams = Vec2(TiledShading_SunSourceDiameter, …)` where
+`constexpr float TiledShading_SunSourceDiameter = 94.0f;` —
+`XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/TiledLightVolumes.h:14`. In `TiledShading.cfi:952-956` the sun takes
+`attenuation = 1.0` and then flows through the identical `lightColor.rgb` multiply as point
+lights. (Note the sun still receives `intensityMul = (1 + 1/94)^2 ≈ 1.021` from
+`TiledLightVolumes.cpp:895-903`.)
+
+> **π asymmetry.** The sun and skybox are divided by π (`TimeOfDay.cpp:471`); local lights are
+> not, yet both feed the same shading term. Three sites manually undo it —
+> `XRenderD3D9/D3DHWShader.cpp:1307-1310` and `:1332-1335`, and
+> `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/VolumetricFog.cpp:2071-2075` — all with the comment
+> `// reconstruct vanilla sun color because it's divided by pi in ConvertIlluminanceToLightColor().`
+> Gated by `r_VolumetricFogSunLightCorrection`, default **1** (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:3265-3269`).
+> A sun authored at *X* lux and a point light authored to deliver *X* lux at 1 m therefore differ
+> by π — **1.65 stops**.
+
+Legacy migration for pre-CE-3.8.2 TOD files: `Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:348-378`,
+`sunIntensity = sunMult * sunColorLum * hdrMult * 10000.0f * gf_PI` with
+`HDRDynamicMultiplier = 2.0f` (`CryCommon/Cry3DEngine/I3DEngine.h:43`). The only .tod shipped in
+this tree (`Editor/asset_thumbnail.tod`) is in that legacy format.
+
+### D9c. Sky — two independent, non-interoperable systems
+
+**Skybox (photometric).** `Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:309-314`, notably
+`:312 AddVar("Skybox", "Intensity (lux)", …, PARAM_SKYBOX_INTENSITY, TYPE_FLOAT, 19800.0f, 0.0f, 20000.0f);`
+Applied at `Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:1187-1189` through the same
+`ConvertIlluminanceToLightColor`. Then:
+
+```cpp
+// Translate to kilo-scale
+m_SkyInfo.m_vSkyBoxEmittance *= (RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE / 1000.0f);   // Renderer.cpp:4006-4007  (×10)
+...
+m_SkyInfo.m_vSkyBoxEmittance += pShaderResources->GetFinalEmittance().toVec3();  // Renderer.cpp:4032
+```
+
+Uploaded at `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/Sky.cpp:150-152`, consumed by
+`Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Stars.cfx:234-239`. Net: `skyBoxExposure = lux / (1000·π)`;
+default 19 800 lux → **6.303**.
+
+> **Scale collision at `Common/Renderer.cpp:4032`.** The TOD term has just been scaled *up* ×10
+> into "kilo-scale", while `GetFinalEmittance()` (`Common/Shaders/ShaderResources.h:104-108`)
+> scales *down* ×0.1 into internal units. The two addends differ by **100×**. No comment
+> reconciles this. Reported as observed, not as confirmed intent.
+
+`m_fSkyBoxMultiplier` / `E3DPARAM_SKYBOX_MULTIPLIER` is dead: set at
+`Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:1338-1340`, defaulted under the "Obsolete" group at
+`Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:424`, uploaded as `SkyDome_SkyBoxParams.z`
+(`Sky.cpp:146-148`), and **never read by any shader** (only struct copies in `SkyCommon.cfi`).
+`SkyHDR.cfx:67-71` is a bare texture passthrough (`SkyHDR.cfx:8`
+`// TODO: remove after old graphics pipeline is removed.`).
+
+**Procedural (Nishita) sky — not photometric.** `Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:316-321`:
+`PARAM_SKYLIGHT_SUN_INTENSITY` (TYPE_COLOR, 1,1,1) and
+`PARAM_SKYLIGHT_SUN_INTENSITY_MULTIPLIER` (default **50.0**, 0…1000). Passed through at
+`Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:1234-1239` → `Cry3DEngine/3dEngine.cpp:1685-1696` (pure store). The
+code-side defaults differ (`Cry3DEngine/SkyLightManager.h:19-23`,
+`Cry3DEngine/SkyLightNishita.cpp:110`, `:118`), and the editor's Mie/Rayleigh values are rescaled
+by 1e-4 at `Cry3DEngine/SkyLightManager.cpp:133-134` with the comment
+*"scale mie and rayleigh scattering for more convenient editing"*. Geometry units are documented
+(`SkyLightNishita.cpp:15-20`, km / km⁻¹) but **`m_sunIntensity` has no documented physical unit**
+and `RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE` appears in none of the SkyLight files. **This path is on an
+arbitrary scale and cannot be reconciled with the photometric one from source.**
+
+`e_SkyType` (`Cry3DEngine/cvars.cpp:859-860`, default 1) only picks the sky *material* spec
+(`CryCommon/Cry3DEngine/I3DEngine.h:1038-1044`, `TimeOfDay.cpp:1199-1207`); it has no intensity
+role. `e_SkyBox` (`cvars.cpp:104-105`, default 1) is on/off.
+
+**Night sky.** Colours `Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:324-325`
+(horizon (222,148,47)/255, zenith (17,38,78)/255); multipliers `:335-336`
+(horizon **0.0001**, zenith **0.00002**, both range 0…0.1) and `:337` (moon **0.01**). Applied at
+`Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp:1060-1064` (each × `m_fHDRMultiplier`) and `:1241-1247`. These raw
+multipliers *are* the night level, in engine units directly.
+
+**Ambient.** There is **no TOD ambient parameter** in 5.7. `E3DPARAM_SKY_COLOR` (the outdoor
+clip-volume ambient) is settable only from Lua —
+`CryScriptSystem/ScriptBindings/ScriptBind_System.cpp:1624` — and defaults to black:
+`Cry3DEngine/ObjMan.cpp:793` `m_vSkyColor.Set(0, 0, 0);`. Consumed at `ClipVolumes.cpp:272`.
