+### D9d. Emissive materials — the kcd/m² chain, traced
+
+**UI.** `Code/Sandbox/EditorQt/Material/MaterialDialog.cpp:449-451`
+(`AddVariable(tableLighting, emissiveIntensity, "Emissive Intensity (kcd/m2)"); …
+emissiveIntensity->SetLimits(0, 200, 1, true, false);`), stored at `:733`
+`sr.m_LMaterial.m_Emittance = ColorF(emissiveCol, emissiveIntensity);`.
+New editor: `Code/Sandbox/Plugins/MaterialEditorPlugin/MaterialProperties.cpp:318-323` — note the
+colour is sRGB-decoded (`col.srgb2rgb();`) but the **intensity is not**; slider 0…200 kcd/m²,
+numerically unbounded above.
+
+**Storage.** `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IShader.h:407`
+`ColorF m_Emittance;  //!< RGB: Color, Alpha: Intensity (kcd/m2 or kilonits).`
+Default `IShader.h:391` `m_Emittance(1, 1, 1, 0),` — intensity 0 = off; gate at `IShader.h:1366`.
+.mtl round-trip `Cry3DEngine/MaterialHelpers.cpp:646-648`, `:672`; legacy `GlowAmount` migration
+`MaterialHelpers.cpp:817-818` with
+`const float legacyIntensityScale = 10.0f;  // Legacy scale factor 10000 divided by 1000 for kilonits`.
+
+**To the constant buffer, unconverted.** `Common/Shaders/ShaderResources.cpp:264`
+`pDst[REG_PM_EMISSIVE_COL] = lm.m_Emittance;` with
+`#define REG_PM_EMISSIVE_COL (2 + EFTT_MAX * 2)` (`Common/Shaders/Shader.h:48`); uploaded at
+`ShaderResources.cpp:785`, bound `:814` at `eConstantBufferShaderSlot_PerMaterial`. Declared in
+HLSL at `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/FXConstantDefs.cfi:44` (`MatEmissiveColor`, register
+`c30` per `:20`).
+
+**The conversion constant — duplicated, CPU and GPU.**
+
+CPU, `Code/CryEngine/RenderDll/Common/Shaders/ShaderResources.h:104-108`:
+
+```cpp
+virtual ColorF GetFinalEmittance() final
+{
+	const float kKiloScale = 1000.0f;
+	return GetColorValue(EFTT_EMITTANCE) * GetStrengthValue(EFTT_EMITTANCE) * (kKiloScale / RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE);
+}
+```
+
+GPU, `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Illum.cfx:653` (identical literal at
+`MultiLayeredMaterials.cfx:1117`):
+
+```hlsl
+half3 emittance = MatEmissiveColor.xyz * MatEmissiveColor.w * (1000.0 / 10000.0);
+```
+
+**The factor is 1000/10000 = 0.1**, i.e. `engine_value = kcd/m² × 0.1 = (cd/m²) / RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE`.
+**No /π.** Critically, `GetFinalEmittance()` is never used for regular geometry — its only
+callers are `Common/Renderer.cpp:4032` (skybox), `Common/RendElements/CREParticle.cpp:677`
+(particles), `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/PostEffects.cpp:1972` and
+`Common/PostProcess/PostProcessHud3D.cpp:691` (HUD3D glow), and
+`XRenderD3D9/D3D_SVO/VoxelSegment.cpp:1767` (SVOGI). For meshes the constant is a **magic literal
+in HLSL**; if `RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE` ever changed, the shaders would silently desync.
+
+Map / gamma: `Illum.cfx:87-96` (`EmittanceMapGamma`, UI 1.0…2.0, default 1.0) and
+`Illum.cfx:599-611` (`GetEmittanceMask`, which reshapes with
+`pow(max(GetLuminance(...), 1e-6), EmittanceMapGamma - 1)` and multiplies by alpha). Default
+texture is white (`Common/Textures/TextureHelpers.cpp:42`).
+
+Output: `Illum.cfx:653-665` — if `bEmissive && MatDifColor.w == 1` the shader **returns
+`emittance` alone**; otherwise `Illum.cfx:695` `OUT.Color.rgb = diffuseAcc + specularAcc + emittance;`.
+**Emissive is not in the G-buffer at all** — `CommonZPass.cfi`, `shadeLib.cfi` and
+`DeferredShading.cfx` contain no emittance references. Emissive objects are re-queued into the
+forward-opaque list (`Common/RenderView.cpp:1618`, `:1652-1654`) and drawn additively:
+`XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/SceneForward.cpp:544-551`
+(`GS_BLSRC_ONE | GS_BLDST_ONE | GS_NOCOLMASK_A`).
+
+There is no symbol `m_fEmissiveIntensity` anywhere in the tree; intensity lives only as
+`m_Emittance.a`.
+
+### D9e. Fog / volumetric
+
+**Fog volume emission** is the only photometric fog quantity:
+`CryDefaultEntities/Module/DefaultComponents/Effects/FogComponent.h:57-58` (label
+`"Specifies how much luminance (kcd/m2) the fog emits."`, `Range<0,100>`, default 0), converted at
+`:148-153` with the same `kiloScale / RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE` idiom. Same idiom in
+`CryCommon/CryEntitySystem/Examples/LoadFogVolume.cpp:15-26`,
+`CryEntitySystem/ScriptBind_Entity.cpp:7723-7727`, `Cry3DEngine/ParticleEffect.cpp:561-562`,
+`Cry3DEngine/ParticleSystem/Features/FeatureAppearance.cpp:302-303` and `:331` (UI label
+`"Emissive (kcd/m2)"` at `:351`). Reaches the GPU unscaled at `VolumetricFog.cpp:1758` →
+`Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/VolumeLighting.cfi:898`.
+
+**Fog colour / albedo are not in light units.** `Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:261-262`,
+`:265-266`, `:271-272` — colours default (0,0,0) with multipliers default **0.0** (range 0…16), so
+**legacy fog is fully off by default**. `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/Fog.cpp` contains no
+`RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE` and no `kiloScale`. VolFog2 albedo defaults are at
+`EnvironmentPreset.cpp:288-307`, repacked without conversion at `TimeOfDay.cpp:1383-1398`; the
+albedo multiplies the *sun colour* (`XRenderD3D9/D3DHWShader.cpp:1301-1310`), it is not itself a
+light unit.
+
+Density scaling is avowedly empirical: `D3DHWShader.cpp:1384`
+`globalDensity *= 0.01f;   // multiply by 1/100 to scale value editor value back to a reasonable range`;
+`VolumetricFog.cpp:1724` `* 0.1f// scale density to volumetric fog.`; `:1735` `* 0.015625f`.
+Legacy per-volume HDR knob still live at `Cry3DEngine/FogVolumeRenderNode.cpp:325`.
+
+### D9f. Is there one consistent engine luminance unit?
+
+**Nominally yes: `1.0 engine unit = 10 000 cd/m² (luminance) or 10 000 lux (illuminance)`.**
+
+* `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IRenderer.h:777-778`
+  `//! Scale factor between photometric and internal light units.` /
+  `const float RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE = 10000.0f;`
+* `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/ToneMapping.cpp:264-267` prints
+  `"Average Luminance (cd/m2)"` as `fLuminance * RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE` and
+  `"Estimated Illuminance (lux)"` likewise.
+* `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IShader.h:407` `(kcd/m2 or kilonits)`.
+* The tone-mapper is a genuine ISO-100 photographic model — `HDRPostProcess.cfx:801-816`
+  (§C5), with the comments *"Compute EV with ISO 100 and standard camera settings"* (`:803`) and
+  *"Compute maximum luminance based on Saturation Based Film Sensitivity (ISO 100, lens factor
+  q=0.65)"* (`:812`).
+
+**Six things break the single-unit story in practice:**
+
+1. Point / projector / area lights carry **no unit at all** (§D9a).
+2. The sun and skybox are divided by π; local lights are not (`TimeOfDay.cpp:471`), and three
+   sites manually undo it.
+3. The Nishita procedural sky is on an **entirely separate arbitrary scale** (§D9c).
+4. Skybox emittance and material emittance are summed at scales **100× apart**
+   (`Common/Renderer.cpp:4032`).
+5. The kcd→engine factor is duplicated as a **literal `(1000.0 / 10000.0)` in HLSL**
+   (`Illum.cfx:653`, `MultiLayeredMaterials.cfx:1117`) rather than shared with
+   `LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE` (which already exists at `HDRPostProcess.cfx:799` but is not shared).
+6. Fog density scaling (`×0.01`, `×0.1`, `×0.015625`) is explicitly "reasonable range" tuning,
+   not unit conversion.
+
+### D10. Dynamic range of shipped defaults
+
+All values in engine units (× 10 000 for cd/m² or lux).
+
+| Source | Authored default | Engine units | Photometric |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **Sun** | 119 000 lux, colour (1, .9725, .9725) — `EnvironmentPreset.cpp:258`, `:257` | 119000/10000/π = **3.788** | 119 000 lux |
+| Sun max slider | 550 000 lux — `EnvironmentPreset.cpp:258` | 17.51 | |
+| **Skybox** | 19 800 lux — `EnvironmentPreset.cpp:312` | 0.630, ×10 at `Renderer.cpp:4007` → **6.303** as the texture multiplier | 19 800 lux |
+| **Point light (default)** | colour (1,1,1) × diffMult 1.0, bulb 0.1 m — `ILightComponent.h:74-76`, `:58` | **1.0** at 1 m from the bulb surface (`TiledLightVolumes.cpp:895-903` ×121; `shadeLib.cfi:199-204` ÷121) | 10 000 lux @ 1 m |
+| Point light max slider | 10 000 — `ILightComponent.h:75` | 10 000 | 10⁸ lux |
+| **Ambient (global)** | `m_vSkyColor(0,0,0)` — `Cry3DEngine/ObjMan.cpp:793` | **0.0** (probes only) | — |
+| **Emissive material** | intensity 0, slider 0…200 kcd/m² — `IShader.h:391`, `MaterialDialog.cpp:451` | 0 … **20.0** (×0.1) | 0 … 200 000 cd/m² |
+| **Fog emission** | 0, `Range<0,100>` kcd/m² — `FogComponent.h:58` | 0 … 10.0 | 0 … 100 000 cd/m² |
+| **Legacy fog colour** | colour 0, multiplier 0 — `EnvironmentPreset.cpp:261-262` | **0.0 (off)** | — |
+| **Night sky horizon** | (222,148,47)/255 × 0.0001 — `EnvironmentPreset.cpp:324`, `:335` | ≈ **6.1e-5** | ≈ 0.61 cd/m² |
+| **Night sky zenith** | (17,38,78)/255 × 0.00002 — `EnvironmentPreset.cpp:325`, `:336` | ≈ **2.9e-6** | ≈ 0.029 cd/m² |
+| **Light cutoff** | `ILLUMINANCE_THRESHOLD 0.004f` — `IShader.h:2063`, `Cry3DEngine/cvars.cpp:888` | 0.004 | 40 lux |
+
+Implied ranges:
+
+* Sun ÷ default point light = 3.788 → **1.92 stops** (in engine units). Compared
+  *photometrically* (119 000 lux vs 10 000 lux @ 1 m) it is **3.57 stops** — the 1.65-stop gap is
+  exactly the π.
+* Sun ÷ night-sky zenith ≈ 1.3 × 10⁶ → **≈ 20.3 stops** of authored day↔night range.
+* Sun ÷ light cutoff ≈ 947 → **≈ 9.9 stops** before a light is culled.
+* Emissive headroom above the sun: 20.0 / 3.788 → **+2.4 stops**.
+
+Sanity against the exposure window (EV 4.5…17.0, §C5): the default sun scene sits at
+`log2(119000 · 100 / 330) ≈ 15.1 EV`, comfortably inside; a point-light-only interior at
+10 000 lux sits at ≈ 11.6 EV.
