+## E. Capture and output
+
+### E11. The frame-capture path
+
+**Cvars** — all registered in CrySystem, `Code/CryEngine/CrySystem/SystemInit.cpp:5072-5077`:
+`capture_frames` (`:5072`), `capture_folder` (`:5073`, default `"CaptureOutput"`),
+`capture_file_format` (`:5074`, default `"jpg"`), `capture_frame_once` (`:5075`),
+`capture_file_name` (`:5076`), `capture_file_prefix` (`:5077`).
+
+There is **no `capture_buffer` cvar**. CryMovie's capture-key buffer enum has one member —
+`CryCommon/CryMovie/AnimKey.h:687` `eCaptureBuffer_Color,`. Renderer-side cached pointers at
+`Common/RendererCVars.h:692-697`, cached by `CacheCaptureCVars`
+(`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:3397`). Track View drives the cvars from
+`Code/CryEngine/CryMovie/Movie.cpp:1440-1461`.
+
+**Writer — one function, three formats, all 8-bit.** `CD3D9Renderer::RT_StoreTextureToFile` —
+`XRenderD3D9/DriverD3D.cpp:1185`:
+
+* `:1199` `byte* pDest = new byte[w * h * 3]; // 3 eight bit channels`
+* `:1206` `::WriteTGA(pDest, w, h, szFilePath, 3*8, 3*8)`
+* `:1209` `::WriteJPG(pDest, w, h, szFilePath, 3*8, 90)`
+* `:1212` `::WritePNG(pDest, w, h, szFilePath)`
+
+The format enum `SCaptureFormatInfo::ECaptureFileFormat`
+(`CryCommon/CryMovie/AnimKey.h:656-659`, extensions `:666-670`) offers only `tga` / `jpg` / `png`.
+Low-level writers: `Common/Textures/Image/TgaImage.cpp:113`,
+`Common/Textures/Image/JpgImage.cpp:411`, `Common/Textures/Image/PngImage.cpp:30`,
+`Common/Textures/Image/DDSImage.cpp:617` (`WriteDDS`, reachable only via
+`Common/Renderer.cpp:1240`, which forces an 8-bit source at `:1262`), and
+`Common/Textures/Image/TifImage.cpp:9` (`WriteTIF`).
+
+**There is no BMP, Radiance `.hdr`, or OpenEXR writer anywhere.** `OpenEXR`, `tinyexr`,
+`stbi_write*` and `.exr` return zero hits across `Code/CryEngine`, `Code/Sandbox`,
+`Code/CryPlugins` and `Engine/Shaders`. The `"hdr"` hits in the renderer (e.g.
+`Common/Renderer.cpp:1401`) are *input* texture-extension checks.
+
+**Which buffer:** the presented swap-chain back buffer — **after** tone-map, **after** the sRGB
+encode, **after** PostAA, **after** UI/HUD/aux geometry.
+
+* `CD3D9Renderer::CaptureFrameBuffer()` — `DriverD3D.cpp:1224`; source at `:1267`
+  `RT_StoreTextureToFile(path, GetActiveDisplayContext()->GetPresentedBackBuffer())`.
+* `CD3D9Renderer::RT_ScreenShot()` — `DriverD3D.cpp:3694`; source `:3704`, written `:3810`.
+* `m_pBackBufferPresented` is assigned in `PrePresent()` — `Common/RenderDisplayContext.cpp:613`,
+  called from `DriverD3D.cpp:3345` / `:3430`.
+* Capture is deliberately one frame late — `DriverD3D.cpp:3336-3338`
+  `// Capture previously presented back-buffer to not cause syncing CPU with GPU…`.
+
+**The readback itself forces 8 bits**, so repointing the source at a float texture would not help:
+`CD3D9Renderer::RT_ReadTexture` — `DriverD3D.cpp:3860`, with `:3867`
+`ETEX_Format dstTexFormat = dstFormat == EReadTextureFormat::BGR8 ? eTF_B8G8R8A8 : eTF_R8G8B8A8;`
+and a stretch-blit into that temp at `:3869-3874`.
+
+**The one float path that exists** is environment-probe cubemap generation, not frame capture:
+
+* `CTexture::RenderEnvironmentCMHDR` — `XRenderD3D9/D3DTexture.cpp:800`; render target
+  `eTF_R16G16B16A16F` at `:810`; half-float readback at `:906-908`.
+* **Tone-mapping is bypassed:** `D3DTexture.cpp:850` sets `SHDF_CUBEMAPGEN`, and
+  `StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:467` `if (!(m_renderingFlags & SHDF_CUBEMAPGEN))` guards the whole
+  HDR-post + PostAA block. So this is genuinely linear scene light.
+* Written as **float TIFF**:
+  `Code/CryPlugins/CryDefaultEntities/Module/DefaultComponents/Lights/EnvironmentProbeComponent.h:229`
+  `WriteTIFToDisk(..., 2, 4, true, "HDRCubemap_highQ", outputPath)` → `Common/Renderer.cpp:1457`,
+  `:1462` → `Common/Textures/Image/TifImage.cpp:33`
+  `TIFFSetField(tif, TIFFTAG_SAMPLEFORMAT, SAMPLEFORMAT_IEEEFP);`.
+
+`r_GetScreenShot`'s help text mentions *"together with .HDR if enabled"*
+(`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:2877`) but **nothing branches on the value** —
+`DriverD3D.cpp:3472-3476` simply calls `ScreenShot()` and resets it. That companion file does not
+exist in 5.7.1.
+
+Variant paths:
+
+* **Stereo**: `DriverD3D.cpp:3806` → `CD3DStereoRenderer::TakeScreenshot`
+  (`XRenderD3D9/D3DStereo.cpp:979`), which uses `GetCurrentBackBuffer()` (`:993-994`) rather than
+  the presented one, and the same 8-bit writer (`:997-998`). (`DriverD3D.cpp:3730` still carries
+  the stale comment `// CaptureFrameBufferToFile must be fixed for 64-bit stereo screenshots`;
+  that function no longer exists.)
+* **High-res panorama / terrain map** (`e_ScreenShot*`, Windows only):
+  `Cry3DEngine/3DEngineRender.cpp:568`; 8-bit RGB buffer `:516`; source
+  `ReadFrameBuffer(..., false, dstFormat)` (`:3479`; `false` = *current*, not presented, back
+  buffer — see `DriverD3D.cpp:3849`); writers `3DEngineRender.cpp:165` (`WriteDDS` as **BC3**),
+  `:167` (TGA 24-bit), `:169` (JPG).
+* **Omni / 360 in-pipeline** (`COmniCameraStage`) writes no file; the cube array inherits the
+  colour target's format — `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/OmniCamera.cpp:24`.
+* **`ICaptureFrameListener` fast path**: interface `CryCommon/CryRenderer/IRenderer.h:82`,
+  `CaptureFrameBufferFast(unsigned char* pDstRGB8, …)` declared `IRenderer.h:1504`, implemented
+  `DriverD3D.cpp:3962` (source `GetPresentedBackBuffer()` `:3971`, BGRA→RGB8 `:4029-4031`).
+  Only in-tree consumer: Statoscope (`CrySystem/Statoscope.h:652`).
+
