+## G. Volumetric fog and SVOGI as HDR contributors
+
+### G14. Volumetric fog
+
+**Stage:** `CVolumetricFogStage` — `XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/VolumetricFog.cpp`. Executed from
+`StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:416-417`, i.e. **before** the transparent passes and long before the
+HDR post chain; the result is applied through the fog pass (`StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:419-420`).
+
+**It is off by default:** `Cry3DEngine/cvars.cpp:100-101`
+`REGISTER_CVAR(e_VolumetricFog, 0, VF_REQUIRE_APP_RESTART, "Activates volumetric fog");` — and the
+switch requires an application restart. The legacy fog path is likewise inert at defaults
+(colour 0, multiplier 0, §D9e), so **a stock scene has no fog contribution at all**.
+
+**Volume formats** — `VolumetricFog.cpp:246-248` (declaration) and `:329-333` (resize):
+
+| Volume | Line(s) | Format | Holds |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `m_pVolFogBufDensityColor` | `:252`, `:442` | **`eTF_R11G11B10F`** | fog albedo × density — **no sign, 6/6/5 mantissa** |
+| `m_pVolFogBufDensity` | `:256`, `:446` | `eTF_R16F` | density scalar |
+| `m_pVolFogBufEmissive` | `:260`, `:450` | **`eTF_R11G11B10F`** | **the kcd/m² fog emission lands here** |
+| `m_pInscatteringVolume` | `:453` | `GetHDRFormat(false,false)` = R16G16B16A16F | in-scattering |
+| `m_pFogInscatteringVolume[0..1]` | `:458` | same | **temporal reprojection history** |
+| `m_pFogDensityVolume[0..1]` | `:471` | `eTF_R16F` | history density (only when the inscattering format has no alpha, `:466`) |
+| `CRendererResources::s_ptexVolumetricFog` | `:531` | `eTF_R16G16B16A16F` | the final applied volume |
+
+So **two of the three injection volumes are R11G11B10F** — fog albedo and fog emission both lose
+sign and precision before any lighting is done.
+
+**A fixed-range encoding on in-scattering.** `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/VolumeLighting.cfi:19`:
+
+```hlsl
+#define VOLUMETRIC_FOG_RANGE_SHIFT_INSCATTER			(16.0f)
+```
+
+applied at `:114-117` `vfEncodeInscattering(rawVal) { return rawVal.xyz * 16.0f; }` (used at
+`:2037` before the UAV write at `:2042`/`:2044`) and undone at `:119-122`
+`vfDecodeInscattering` (used at `:2102`, `:2175`, `:2286`, `:2430-2431`). **This is a hard
+assumption about the numeric range of engine light units** — a ×16 shift chosen to place fog
+in-scattering in the useful part of the float range. A global pre-exposure or a unit rescale
+invalidates it.
+
+**Every intensity multiplier / clamp on the fog colour path:**
+
+| # | file:line | What | Affects |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `VolumetricFog.cpp:1043` | `const float itensityScale = rd->m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer;` — the pre-exposure hook (§C7), hard-wired 1.0 | **colour** (all fog lights) |
+| 2 | `VolumetricFog.cpp:2070-2075` | `sunColor *= gf_PI;` under `r_VolumetricFogSunLightCorrection` (default **1**, `Common/RendererCVars.cpp:3265-3269`), comment `// reconstruct vanilla sun color because it's divided by pi in ConvertIlluminanceToLightColor().` | **colour** — the π asymmetry of §D9b, undone here |
+| 3 | `VolumetricFog.cpp:1724` | `const float globalDensity = fvol.m_globalDensity * 0.1f;// scale density to volumetric fog.` | density (indirectly colour) |
+| 4 | `VolumetricFog.cpp:1735` | `Vec3 cHeightFallOffDirScaledVec(fvol.m_heightFallOffDirScaled * 0.015625f);  // scale fall off ramp to volumetric fog.` | density |
+| 5 | `VolumetricFog.cpp:1752-1753` | `const float normalizeFactor = (1.0f / (1.0f + 0.5f));` on noise scale | density |
+| 6 | `VolumetricFog.cpp:1758` | `injectInfo.emission = fvol.m_emission;` — passed through unscaled (already converted on the CPU, §D9e) | **colour** |
+| 7 | `VolumeLighting.cfi:661` | `float fogDensityAtWorldPos = saturate(fogDensityAtCamera * fogDensityDifference);// limit maximum fog density.` | density (mask) |
+| 8 | `VolumeLighting.cfi:883` | `fogInt = saturate(densityNoise * fv.globalDensity.x * (fogInt - fv.densityOffset.x));` | density (mask) |
+| 9 | `VolumeLighting.cfi:897-898` | `densityColor += fv.fogColor.xyz * fogInt; emissive += fv.emission.xyz * fogInt;` — the accumulation, **unclamped** but written into R11G11B10F at `:993` (`VolumetricFogEmissiveOutput[…] = emissive.rgb;`, UAV declared `:678`) | **colour** |
+| 9b | `VolumeLighting.cfi:2034` | `inscatter += VolumetricFogEmissiveInput[DispatchThreadID.xyz].xyz;` (SRV `:1427`) — emission joins in-scattering **before** the ×16 encode at `:2037` | **colour** |
+| 10 | `VolumeLighting.cfi:2112` | `float muE = max(0.000000001f, extinctionCoefficient * density.x);` | divisor guard |
+| 11 | `VolumeLighting.cfi:2298`, `:2440` | `prev.xyz = isfinite(prev.xyz) ? prev.xyz : float3(0,0,0);` — NaN/Inf rejection in the temporal filter | colour |
+| 12 | **`VolumeLighting.cfi:2444-2459`** | the temporal filter's **luminance-similarity history rejection** — see below | **colour, scale-dependent** |
+
+Item 12 is the one that matters most for a rescale. `VolumeLighting.cfi:2444-2459`:
+
+```hlsl
+float pl = GetLuminance(prev.xyz);                                              // :2444
+float cpl = clamp(pl, minl, maxl);                                              // :2445
+const float ratio = 0.1f;// from 0.1 to 0.3f is good due to less ghosting.      // :2446
+float diff = pl - cpl;                                                          // :2448
+float w = diff > 0.0f ? -24.0f : 48.0f;                                         // :2449
+float similarityFactor = saturate(exp2(w * diff));                              // :2450
+float cl = GetLuminance(current.xyz);                                           // :2453
+similarityFactor = min(similarityFactor, lerp(0.6f, 1.0f, saturate(exp2(-8.0f * abs(pl - cl))))); // :2454
+blendFactor *= lerp(similarityFactor, 1.0f, ratio);                             // :2459
+```
+
+`minl` / `maxl` are the Rec.709 luminance bounds over the 5×5×5 voxel neighbourhood
+(`VolumeLighting.cfi:2335-2391`, seeded with `vfEncodeInscattering(65504.0f)` at `:2335` — the
+fp16 max), decoded back at `:2430-2431`. **The exponents `-24.0f`, `48.0f` and `-8.0f` operate on
+an absolute luminance *difference*, not a ratio**, so they encode a fixed expectation about how
+large a "large" fog luminance is in engine units. Multiplying all lights by a pre-exposure factor
+changes how aggressively the fog temporal filter rejects history — brighter → total rejection
+(flicker), darker → no rejection (ghosting). It also uses `GetLuminance` (Rec.709), so a
+709→AP1 change shifts it too.
+
+**Legacy (non-volumetric) fog.** Colour is not in light units at all (§D9e): TOD fog colour
+defaults (0,0,0) with multiplier **0.0** (`Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:261-262`), so legacy
+fog is off by default. Density scaling `XRenderD3D9/D3DHWShader.cpp:1144` and `:1385`
+`globalDensity *= 0.01f;   // multiply by 1/100 to scale value editor value back to a reasonable range`;
+the radial gradient uses magic `14.0f` / `1/21` at `D3DHWShader.cpp:1195-1197`. The fog stage
+passes `Vec4(m_vSceneLuminanceInfo.x, m_fAdaptedSceneScale, 0, 0)` as `HDRParams2`
+(`XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/Fog.cpp:236-239`) — **both hard-wired to 1.0** (§C7). In fact that
+constant is entirely dead: `HDRParams2` occurs exactly once in the whole tree, at
+`Fog.cpp:238`, and **no shader declares or reads it** (grep over `Engine/Shaders/` returns
+nothing).
+
+**The apply pass adds no colour clamp.** `HDRPostProcess.cfx:1562-1599` `FogPassPS`:
+`localFogColor.a = saturate(localFogColor.a)` at `:1582` and `:1589`/`:1593` are **alpha only**;
+the colour goes out through `HDROutput(OUT, localFogColor, 1)` at `:1596`, and `HDROutput` is a
+pure passthrough — `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/ShadeLib.cfi:1353-1356` `{ OUT.Color = Color; }`.
+
+The TOD **"Final density clamp"** (`Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:277` legacy, `:307`
+volumetric, both default **1.0**, range 0…1) becomes `pFogParams.w = 1.0f - clamp_tpl(clampTransmittance, 0, 1)`
+(`XRenderD3D9/D3DHWShader.cpp:1358`, `:1390`) → `params.clampTransmittance = vfHeightDensityParams.w`
+(`VolumetricFog.cfi:390`) → `VolumetricFog.cfi:702-710`
+`volumetricFog.xyz = volumetricFog.xyz * (1.0f - params.clampTransmittance);`. **At the default
+1.0 it resolves to a no-op**; lower values scale the fog colour down and floor the transmittance.
+
+**Units relative to lights and sun:** fog *emission* is on the photometric scale (kcd/m² ×0.1,
+§D9e); fog *lights* inherit whatever the tiled light list carries, including the same missing-unit
+problem as local lights (§D9a); the fog *sun* is explicitly π-corrected back to "vanilla"
+(`VolumetricFog.cpp:2070-2075`) while the deferred sun is not — so **fog and deferred lighting do
+not agree on the sun's magnitude by a factor of π**.
+
+### G15. SVOGI / total illumination
+
+**It is off by default and off the default render path.** `CSvoRenderer::IsActive()` —
+`XRenderD3D9/D3D_SVO.cpp:1655-1658` `return CSvoRenderer::s_pInstance && CSvoRenderer::s_pInstance->e_svoTI_Apply;`.
+`e_svoTI_Apply` defaults to **0** (`Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTreeCVars.inl:211`) and is driven from the
+level's Total Illumination settings, whose `active` default is `false`
+(`Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDayConstants.cpp:186`, applied at `Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTree.cpp:2281`).
+`e_svoTI_Active` is likewise 0 (`SceneTreeCVars.inl:66`), as are `e_svoEnabled`
+(`SceneTreeCVars.inl:34`). **There is no `e_GI` cvar in this tree.**
+
+**Screen-space targets are all fp16.** `CSvoRenderer::CheckAllocateRT` allocates every RT as
+`eTF_R16G16B16A16F` — diffuse/specular radiance `D3D_SVO.cpp:1069`, `:1076`; ALD (light direction)
+`:1067`, `:1074`; `SVO_NID` `:1085`; air min/max `:1086-1087`; shadow `:1091-1093`; the sixteen
+de-mosaic targets `:1097-1118`; and the final outputs `tsDiff.pRT_FIN_OUT_0/1` (`:1106-1107`) and
+`tsSpec.pRT_FIN_OUT_0/1` (`:1120-1121`). **No R11G11B10F anywhere in `CSvoRenderer`.** The four
+RSM maps are the exception: `SVO_SUN_RSM_COLOR` (`D3D_SVO.cpp:1935`), `SVO_SUN_RSM_NORML`
+(`:1958`) and the projector pools (`:1943`, `:1966`) are **`eTF_R8G8B8A8`**.
+
+**The voxel pools are 8-bit.** `Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTree.cpp:939`
+`m_voxTexFormat = eTF_R8G8B8A8; // eTF_BC3` (also `:36`). Every brick pool — opacity, albedo,
+direct light, bounces 2/3/4, normals, ALDI cache, RT-tris — is created with that format
+(`Cry3DEngine/SVO/VoxelSegment.cpp:1076`, `:1086`, `:1094`, `:1102`, `:1110`, `:1118`, `:1127`,
+`:1134`, `:1151`, `:1166`). The only float pool is the node/tree structure at
+`VoxelSegment.cpp:1156` (`eTF_R32G32B32A32F`) — geometry bounds, not radiance. CPU-side bricks are
+`ColorB` (`VoxelSegment.h:39`). In the default `e_svoTI_IntegrationMode = 0` only the opacity
+subset exists at all (`VoxelSegment.cpp:3553`).
+
+**Where radiance is quantised — four separate places:**
+
+1. **CPU voxelisation → 8-bit, `[0,1]`.** `VoxelSegment.cpp:1877-1880`:
+   ```cpp
+   colOut.r = SATURATEB((int)(vColFin.r * 255.f));   // albedo
+   colOut.g = SATURATEB((int)(vColFin.g * 255.f));
+   colOut.b = SATURATEB((int)(vColFin.b * 255.f));
+   colOut.a = SATURATEB((int)(emiFin * 255.f));      // emissive LUMINANCE
+   ```
+   The emissive term is collapsed to a **scalar** first — `VoxelSegment.cpp:1767`
+   `EmiOutSubSub = +rMI.pMat->…->GetFinalEmittance().Luminance();` — so the SVO has **no coloured
+   emitters**, and an emissive material above 1.0 in engine units (i.e. above 10 000 cd/m²,
+   which is only 10 kcd/m² — well inside the 0…200 authoring slider of §D9d) **saturates to 255
+   here** and survives only as `e_svoTI_EmissiveMultiplier` × 1.0.
+2. **Disk/stream codec → 4 bits per channel with gamma 2.0.**
+   `VoxelSegment.cpp:37` `#define SVO_PACK_TO_16_BIT     true`; save
+   `VoxelSegment.cpp:3432-3438` (`powf(v/255, 1/2)`, then `>> 4` and nibble-packed); load
+   `VoxelSegment.cpp:399-404` (`<< 4`, then `powf(v/255, 2)`). **16 distinct albedo levels survive
+   a disk round-trip.**
+3. **The GPU radiance codec — the hard ceiling.**
+   `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO.cfi:142-152`:
+   ```hlsl
+   float4 EncodeHDR(float3 Color)
+   {
+       float fMax = max(1.f / 4.f, max(max(Color.r, Color.g), Color.b));
+       return float4(Color.xyz / fMax, fMax / 4.f);
+   }
+   float3 DecodeHDR(float4 Color) { Color.rgb = Color.rgb * (Color.a * 4.f); return Color.rgb; }
+   ```
+   packed to 8-bit with `saturate` at `CommonSVO.cfi:294-297` (`FlOAT4_TO_UINT`) and unpacked at
+   `:284`. Because `.a = fMax/4` is stored in a `[0,1]` 8-bit channel, **the maximum representable
+   in-SVO radiance is exactly 4.0** and the minimum scale is 0.25. Anything brighter clips *and*
+   shifts hue — the brightest channel is divided out first, so an over-4.0 pixel converges on its
+   own normalised chromaticity. Writes: `Total_Illumination.cfx:2209-2212` (injection),
+   `:2502-2505` (propagation); read back at `CommonSVO.cfi:896-900`.
+4. **Screen-space output clamps.** `Total_Illumination.cfx:1234-1238`
+   `clamp(lerp(…prev…, OUT.Diffuse, fBlendMin), -8, 8)` on all four cone-trace MRTs, and
+   `Total_Illumination.cfx:2765` `OUT.Diffuse = clamp(lerp(valPrev, OUT.Diffuse, fBlend), 0, 8);`
+   on the final upscale. So despite fp16 targets, **GI radiance reaching `ApplyGI` is limited to
+   8.0** — about 2× the default sun (§D10).
+
+**Light injection scaling.** Lights are collected with **no multiplier at all** —
+`Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTree.cpp:2485-2487` `lightTI.vCol = rLight.m_Color.toVec4();` (dynamic) /
+`m_BaseColor` (static), uploaded verbatim at `D3D_SVO.cpp:944` into `SVO_LightCol0/1`
+(`:926-930`). The sun is an ordinary `DLF_SUN` entry (`SceneTree.cpp:2492-2494`) and additionally
+feeds the RSM: `D3D_SVO.cpp:1844`
+`Vec4 vData(gEnv->p3DEngine->GetSunColor(), e_svoTI_InjectionMultiplier);` → `SVO_RsmSunCol`,
+consumed at `CommonSVO.cfi:1028` `vRGBD.xyz = vSunLight * SVO_RsmSunCol.xyz * SVO_RsmSunCol.w;`
+and `Total_Illumination.cfx:2283`. **`GetSunColor()` is the π-divided TOD sun of §D9b, with no
+correction here** — unlike volumetric fog (§G14), SVOGI does *not* undo the π.
+
+Shader-side scaling chain in `ComputeDirectStaticLighting` (`Total_Illumination.cfx`):
+
+```hlsl
+vRGB.xyz *= SvoParamsInject.x;                          // :2143  e_svoTI_InjectionMultiplier
+vRGB.xyz += pixel.w * SvoParamsMisc.x;                  // :2146  8-bit emissive × EmissiveMultiplier
+vRGB.xyz += max(0, SvoParamsCommon.z * vSkyColorTop.z); // :2149  DiffuseBias — an ADDITIVE constant
+pixel.xyz *= vRGB.xyz;                                  // :2204  × 8-bit voxel albedo
+pixel = EncodeHDR(pixel);                               // :2209  → clipped at 4.0
+```
+
+Propagation (`ComputePropagateLighting`): saturation lerp `:2454`, albedo multiply `:2472`, then
+
+```hlsl
+vCollectedLight.xyz = pow(vCollectedLight.xyz, SvoParamsInject.y); // :2474
+```
+
+where `SvoParamsInject.y = 1.f / max(e_svoTI_PropagationBooster, 0.001f)` (`D3D_SVO.cpp:1435`,
+default booster **1.5** → exponent ≈ 0.667). **A power law is not scale-invariant.**
+
+The traced result is scaled once, at `CommonSVO.cfi:1358-1359`:
+`float fAmplifier = IsDiffuseMode() ? SvoParamsDiffuse.w : SvoParamsSpecular.w; vRgbOut.xyz *= fAmplifier;`
+
+**Sky.** Guarded by `if (GetCVars()->e_svoTI_UseTODSkyColor)` (`SceneTree.cpp:1696`):
