+**Where GI meets the deferred result** — `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/TiledShading.cfi:105-125`:
+
+```hlsl
+if(nIntegrMode == 0)      // AO only
+    specularAcc *= lerp(vSkyLightIrradiance.xyz, 1.f, surfGloss * GetLuminance(surfSpecCol)); // :111
+    diffuseAcc  *= vSkyLightIrradiance.xyz;                                                    // :112
+else if(nIntegrMode == 1)
+    specularAcc *= lerp(min( 2.f, GetLuminance(diffuseIrradiance)
+                  / (GetLuminance(diffuseAcc + diffuseForwAcc) + 0.001)), 1.f, …) * fParms.z;   // :117
+    diffuseAcc = diffuseIrradiance;                                                            // :118
+else if(nIntegrMode == 2) // full GI
+    diffuseAcc  = TexGiDiffuse[pixelCoord];                                                    // :122
+    specularAcc = TexGiSpecular[pixelCoord];                                                   // :123
+```
+
+`TexGiDiffuse` / `TexGiSpecular` are bound from `CSvoRenderer::GetDiffuseFinRT()` /
+`GetSpecularFinRT()` (`XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/TiledShading.cpp:108-110`, defaulting to
+`s_ptexBlack` at `:101-102`, bound to slots 10/11 at `:135-136`; forward path uses slots 46/47,
+`SceneForward.cpp:816-817`). Those are the fp16 `pRT_FIN_OUT_0` targets
+(`D3D_SVO.cpp:1106`, `:1120`), read with an unfiltered integer load. Mode selection arrives via
+`SvoParamsSkyColor.y` (`D3D_SVO.cpp:1456-1475`; `-1` when inactive).
+
+One division hazard: `Total_Illumination.cfx:2735`
+`float4 vFinalDiffuse = tex2DlodPC(sceneDiffuseFin, …) / SvoParamsDiffuse.w * SvoParamsSpecular.w;`
+divides by `e_svoTI_DiffuseAmplifier`, whose UI minimum is **0.0**
+(`Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDayConstants.cpp:266`).
+
+**What caps dynamic range, and what breaks under a light-unit rescale:**
+
+| Rank | Item | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | **The voxel radiance codec** (`CommonSVO.cfi:142-146`, `:291-298`) | Hard ceiling **4.0**, floor 0.25, 8-bit mantissa + 8-bit shared exponent. A pre-exposure *k* > 1 clips *and* hue-shifts every bounce; *k* < 1 collapses values below the 0.25 floor where the codec degenerates to plain 8-bit LDR. **Must be redesigned before any unit rescale.** |
+| 2 | **`pow(radiance, 1/PropagationBooster)`** (`Total_Illumination.cfx:2474`) | `pow(k·L, e) = k^e · pow(L, e)` — bounce gain changes by `k^(e−1)`. Same class: the disk codec's `powf(x, 1/2)` (`VoxelSegment.cpp:3432`) and `CommonSVO.cfi:995` `pow(vAlbe, .75)`. |
+| 3 | **The `[-8,8]` / `[0,8]` screen-space clamps** (`Total_Illumination.cfx:1234-1238`, `:2765`) | Absolute, not exposure-relative. |
+| 4 | **`e_svoTI_DiffuseBias`** (`Total_Illumination.cfx:2149`, `:2745-2748`) | An **additive** term in light units — does not scale with a pre-exposure multiplier, so it becomes either invisible or an overwhelming grey lift. (`e_svoTI_MinReflectance` is in *reflectance* units and is safe.) |
+| 5 | **Absolute magic constants** — `VOX_AIR_ALBEDO_COLOR 0.01f` (`Total_Illumination.cfx:15`, used `:2199`, `:2466`), the fog density `0.001f * VOX_TI_ATMO_DENSITY` (`CommonSVO.cfi:925`) | tuned against the current unit scale |
+| 6 | **`min(2.f, …)` in `ApplyGI` mode 1** (`TiledShading.cfi:117`) | a *ratio*, so scale-invariant **only if GI and deferred diffuse are rescaled identically** — which fails precisely because of item 3 |
+| 7 | **Epsilons** `+0.001` (`TiledShading.cfi:117`), `Total_Illumination.cfx:2653`, `:2671` | stop being negligible under small *k* |
+| 8 | **Sign/packing conventions** — `e_svoTI_SkyColorMultiplier`'s sign is a boolean (`SceneTree.cpp:2304-2305`, `D3D_SVO.h:87`); `lightTI.vCol.w` is a shadow flag (`SceneTree.cpp:2489`) then a light index (`D3D_SVO.cpp:1907`) | a naive `vCol *= k` would corrupt both |
+| 9 | **RSM colour maps are `eTF_R8G8B8A8`** (`D3D_SVO.cpp:1935`, `:1943`, `:1958`, `:1966`) | fine for albedo, but there is no HDR headroom in the RSM itself |
+
+Already safe: the fp16 screen-space chain has ample headroom (only the explicit clamps limit it),
+and the multiplicative amplifiers are pure scalars — though their *usable range* shifts with any
+rescale because they feed items 1 and 2.
+
+### G16. Other lighting-side contributors
+
+#### Sun shafts
+
+Params (`Common/PostProcess/PostEffects.h`): `SunShafts_Amount` **0.25** (`:541`),
+`SunShafts_RaysAmount` **0.25** (`:542`), `SunShafts_RaysAttenuation` **5.0** (`:543`),
+`SunShafts_RaysSunColInfluence` **1.0** (`:544`), `SunShafts_RaysCustomColor` `(1,1,1,1)` (`:545`).
+`r_sunshafts` default **2** (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:2131`, `#define SUNSHAFTS_DEFAULT_VAL 2` at
+`Common/Renderer.h:117`). Gen-pass step sizes are hardcoded at `SunShafts.cpp:121` and `:149`.
+
+**The composition constant throws the sun's magnitude away.** `ToneMapping.cpp:137-140`:
+
+```cpp
+Vec3 sunColor = gEnv->p3DEngine->GetSunColor();
+sunColor.Normalize();                                                    // :138
+sunColor.SetLerp(Vec3(sunShaftParams[0].x, …), sunColor, sunShaftParams[1].w);
+shaftsSunCol = Vec4(sunColor * sunShaftParams[1].z, 1);                   // :140
+```
+
+Only the sun's *hue* survives; shaft brightness is `SunShafts_RaysAmount` alone
+(`PostEffects.h:565`).
+
+**Target format (confirmed):** `SunShafts.cpp:38` returns
+`m_pTexDisplayTargetScaled[GetDownscaledTargetsIndex()]`, allocated at
+`GraphicsPipeline.cpp:289-291` with `nLDRPFormat` (`:283`) = **`eTF_R10G10B10A2` UNORM**; the
+ping-pong temp (`SunShafts.cpp:43`) is the same (`GraphicsPipeline.cpp:297-298`).
+
+Clamps in `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Sunshafts.cfx`:
+
+| Line | Code | Kind |
+|---|---|---|
+| `:141` | `OUT.Color = half4(sceneDepth, sceneDepth, sceneDepth, 1 - sceneDepth.x);` | depth seeds the colour channel |
+| `:144-147` | `half3 sceneCol = …; // comes straight from hdr scaled target` … `OUT.Color.xyz *= dot(sceneCol, 0.33 * 4);` | **unbounded HDR luminance (≈1.32·(R+G+B)) written into a UNORM target — silently clipped at 1.0.** The primary flaw. |
+| `:164` | `float sunDist = saturate(fSign) * saturate(1 - saturate(length(…)*params.y));` | mask/weight |
+| `:196-198` | `accum /= 8.0;` then `OUT.Color = accum * 2 * float4(sunDist.xxx, 1);` | ×2 per gen pass, run twice → ×4, each write re-clipped by UNORM |
+| `:199` | `OUT.Color.w += 1.0 - saturate(saturate(fSign * 0.1 + 0.9));` | alpha |
+
+There is **no explicit `saturate` on shaft colour anywhere** — the clamping is entirely implicit in
+the R10G10B10A2 format. `SunShafts.cpp:61` clamps `RaysAttenuation` to `[0,10]` (a falloff, not
+colour). Composition into the tone-mapped image is at `HDRPostProcess.cfx:964`, i.e. **after** the
+`saturate` at `:871` — sun shafts are entirely display-referred.
+
+**Under a rescale:** shafts are almost fully immune, and that is the defect. `dot(sceneCol, 1.32)`
+is the only place scene luminance enters, and it saturates for any pixel whose R+G+B exceeds ≈0.76
+— with real engine values the mask is already clipped everywhere bright, so scaling lights *up*
+changes nothing while scaling *down* would abruptly make shafts luminance-dependent again. The
+shaft colour is `Normalize()`d so it never tracks sun intensity at all.
+
+#### Screen-space reflections
+
+Cvars (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp`): `r_SSReflections` **0** (`:1789`), `r_SSReflHalfRes` **1**
+(`:1791`), `r_SSReflDistance` **0.25** (`:1793`), `r_SSReflSamples` **28** (`:1797`). Uploaded as
+`g_mSSRParams` at `ScreenSpaceReflections.cpp:77-81`. **There is no brightness multiplier in the
+SSR path.**
+
+Formats: the raytrace/blur/compose chain uses `m_pTexHDRTargetMasked` (`GraphicsPipeline.cpp:241`)
+and `m_pTexHDRTargetMaskedScaled[][]` (`:229-238`), all `nHDRAFormat` — and because
+`withAlpha == true` the R11G11B10F branch of `GetHDRFormat` can never be taken, so these are
+**always `eTF_R16G16B16A16F`**. But the **colour source is `m_pTexHDRTargetPrev[eye]`**
+(`ScreenSpaceReflections.cpp:62`), which is **R11G11B10F** (`GraphicsPipeline.cpp:239-240`).
+
+**There is no temporal accumulation.** The stage is raytrace (`:50-88`), copy (`:91-94`), a
+three-level downsample/blur (`:97-104`) and composition (`:106-132`). No history buffer, no
+`1/(1+luma)` blend. The only temporal element is *reprojection into the previous frame's colour*,
+`Reflection.cfi:565-581`.
+
+**What `m_pTexHDRMeasuredLuminance` is for:** bound at `ScreenSpaceReflections.cpp:63` →
+`SSRRay_HDRLum : register(t5)` (`DeferredShading.cfx:352`), and used once:
+
+```hlsl
+const float fLum = GetTexture2DLod(SSRRay_HDRLum, …).x * 100; // Limit brightness to reduce aliasing of specular highlights   // DeferredShading.cfx:392
+…
+params.maxLum = fLum;                                                                                                          // :411
+```
+
+becoming a hard clamp on the reflected colour at `Reflection.cfi:675` (and `:338` in `SSRaycast`):
+
+```hlsl
+color.rgb = min( isfinite( color.rgb ) ? color.rgb : 0, params.maxLum.xxx );
+```
+
+i.e. **the reflection ceiling is 100 × the scene's geometric-mean luminance** (the `.x` channel of
+the auto-exposure result, §C5). In secondary viewports the clamp collapses to **1.0** —
+`DeferredShading.cfx:394` `const float fLum = 1.0f; // We don't have auto exposure running in secondary viewports`.
+
+Other clamps are weights: `Reflection.cfi:225`/`:365` (`dirAtten`), `:299`/`:589` (edge weights),
+`DeferredShading.cfx:439` (alpha), `:474` (mip blend). Consumption at `TiledShading.cfi:924-925`
+is a plain `lerp`.
+
+**Under a rescale:** SSR is the best-behaved contributor — its one colour clamp is
+exposure-relative and rescales with the lights. Two caveats: the secondary-viewport
+`fLum = 1.0f` branch (`DeferredShading.cfx:394`) is unit-referred and breaks outright; and the
+colour source is R11G11B10F, so a large upward rescale clips *reflected* colour even though the
+fp16 SSR targets would cope.
+
+#### Environment probes / cubemap capture
+
+Authoring: `EnvironmentProbeComponent.h:109-115` (`m_diffuseMultiplier` / `m_specularMultiplier`,
+`Schematyc::Range<0,100>`, default **1.0**), applied at `:407-408` exactly like a point light
+(§D9a), with `light.m_fHDRDynamic = 0.f` at `:410`.
+
+Capture → disk → runtime chain, **fp16 all the way to the compressor**:
+
+1. `XRenderD3D9/D3DTexture.cpp:810` — capture target `eTF_R16G16B16A16F`;
+   `CTexture::RenderEnvironmentCMHDR` at `:800`, half-float readback `:906-916`.
+2. `EnvironmentProbeComponent.h:181`, `:213`, `:217`, `:219` — 16× SSAA downsample, still
+   `CryHalf4`.
+3. `EnvironmentProbeComponent.h:229` — `WriteTIFToDisk(…, 2, 4, true, "HDRCubemap_highQ", …)`,
+   float TIFF.
+4. RC presets — `Code/Tools/RC/rc.ini:62-63` map `HDRCubemap_highQ` →
+   `[EnvironmentProbeHDR]` (`:283-304`, `pixelformat=BC6UH`, `maxtexturesize=256`,
+   `colorspace=linear,linear`) and `HDRDiffuseCubemap_highQ` →
+   `[EnvironmentProbeHDR_Irradiance]` (`:308-326`, `BC6UH`, 32×32). The comments at `:282` and
+   `:307` say "tiled shading requires cubemap to be 256x256 / 32x32 BC6UH".
+   **BC6H *unsigned* — not DXT, not RGBM.**
+5. Runtime atlases — `TiledLightVolumes.cpp:76-82`:
+   `eTF_BC6UH` on desktop, `eTF_R9G9B9E5` on Android; spec array `:87`, diffuse array `:102`.
+6. **Decode at sample time is a no-op** — `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/ShadeLib.cfi:1305-1308`
+   `half4 DecodeHDRCubemap(half4 color) { return color; }`. Used at `TiledShading.cfi:212`,
+   `:222`, `:766`, `:770`, `:780`. No RGBM/RGBE decode remains — probes are natively HDR.
+
+**`m_fProbeAttenuation` does not exist in this tree.** `SortPriority`
+(`EnvironmentProbeComponent.h:84`, `:424`) is purely an ordering key
+(`Common/RenderView.cpp:2427-2428`) deciding which probe consumes the `probeWeightSum` budget
+first. Note `TiledLightVolumes.cpp:842` packs `renderLight.m_Color.a` as the probe strength — and
+`SetLightColor(m_color * m_diffuseMultiplier)` scales alpha too.
+
+**No clamps on probe colour at all** — `TiledShading.cfi:773` and `:781` are pure
+multiply-accumulate; everything saturating nearby (`:746`, `:756`, `:772`, `:161-163`) is a weight.
+
+**Under a rescale:** the runtime path rescales cleanly, but **BC6UH is unsigned** with a 65504
+ceiling, and **baked probes are stored on disk** — rescaling light units silently diverges every
+existing `.dds` probe from live lights by exactly the rescale factor until a full rebake. There is
+no version stamp or compensating multiplier on the stored cubemap. Also note
+`m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` (`TiledLightVolumes.cpp:824`) scales the probe *tint* but not the
+cubemap contents, so using it as the pre-exposure hook would **double-apply to probes** unless the
+bake compensates.
