+//#define ENABLE_REDUCED_COLOR_RANGE
+#define REDUCED_COLOR_RANGE_EXP
+```
+
+`ENABLE_REDUCED_COLOR_RANGE` is **commented out**, so the temporal blend at `:2809` is a plain
+linear `lerp` on raw HDR. (Were it re-enabled, `REDUCED_COLOR_RANGE_EXP` is defined, so it would
+take the `exp2/-log2` branch at `:2800-2801`/`:2813`, not the `c/(1+L)` one — and the `#else`
+inverse at `:2815` divides by `1.0f - L` with `range = 1.0f` at `:2803`, which produces negatives
+and a pole for any L ≥ 1. **Dormant scene-referred landmine.**)
+
+The live temporal clamp is a neighbourhood clip on colour — `Clouds.cfx:2784-2786` — plus NaN
+rejection at `:2789`. Both scale-invariant. The only other colour-relevant clamp is `:3019`.
+
+**Under a rescale:** clouds are clean today (fp16, linear lerp, sun-covariant colour). Risks: the
+R11G11B10F shadow textures, and the dormant reduced-range block.
+
+#### Skybox at draw time
+
+`StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:408` `GetStage<CSkyStage>()->Execute(m_pipelineResources.m_pTexHDRTarget, pZTexture);`
+→ `Sky.cpp:271`, `:338` `m_skyPass.SetRenderTarget(0, pColorTex);` with `:340`
+`SetState(GS_DEPTHFUNC_EQUAL)` (opaque overwrite, no blend). Target is
+**`eTF_R16G16B16A16F`**. Sky-dome scattering LUTs are fp16 too (`Sky.cpp:41-45`).
+
+Constant upload — `Sky.cpp:143-156`:
+
+```cpp
+const float skyBoxMultiplier = …m_SkyInfo.m_fSkyBoxMultiplier; // Deprecated: E3DPARAM_SKYBOX_MULTIPLIER  // :146
+const Vec4 skyBoxParams(skyBoxAngle, skyBoxScaling, skyBoxMultiplier, 0.f);                                // :147
+m_skyPass.SetConstant(skyBoxParamName, skyBoxParams, eHWSC_Pixel);                                         // :148
+const Vec3& skyBoxExposure = …m_SkyInfo.m_vSkyBoxEmittance;                                                // :151
+m_skyPass.SetConstant(skyBoxExposureName, Vec4(skyBoxExposure, 1.0f), eHWSC_Pixel);                        // :152
+```
+
+declared at `Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/SkyCommon.cfi:29-31`. Consumption —
+`Stars.cfx:235-239` uses `SkyDome_SkyBoxParams.x` and `.y` (angle, stretch) and
+`SkyDome_SkyBoxExposure.rgb`. **`SkyDome_SkyBoxParams.z` — the deprecated
+`E3DPARAM_SKYBOX_MULTIPLIER` — is uploaded but read by no shader**, confirming §D9c.
+
+Procedural sky at `Stars.cfx:202`, `:211`, `:220-229`; stars at `:84-87` and `:129-131`, with
+intensity from `Sky.cpp:357` (`E3DPARAM_NIGHSKY_STAR_INTENSITY`), gated `:359`, drawn additively
+`:380`.
+
+**There are no clamps on the sky colour path.** The only `saturate`s in `Stars.cfx` are a UV
+(`:57`) and a gradient blend factor (`:209`). `SkyHDR.cfx:70` is a pass-through. **The sky is the
+one contributor that writes unclamped scene-referred radiance into fp16.**
+
+**Under a rescale, the sky bites hardest.** `Common/Renderer.cpp:4007`
+`m_SkyInfo.m_vSkyBoxEmittance *= (RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE / 1000.0f);` is a **direct function of
+the constant being changed**, and it runs in the *opposite direction* to `GetFinalEmittance()`
+(`ShaderResources.h:107`, ÷10 000) which is added into the same sum at `Renderer.cpp:4032`. Any
+change to `RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE` diverges the two terms by the **square** of the factor —
+they must be fixed together or not at all. Downstream, the unclamped sky is exactly what feeds
+auto-exposure through the hardcoded reflectance assumption at `HDRPostProcess.cfx:745-747`
+(`baseColorLum = 0.2` for zero-albedo pixels), another unit-referred constant.
+
+#### Cross-cutting summary
+
+| Contributor | Writes into | Worst fixed-range encoding | Scale-covariant? |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Sun shafts | `m_pTexDisplayTargetScaled[]` | **R10G10B10A2 UNORM `[0,1]`**, composited post-`saturate` | **No** — `sunColor.Normalize()` discards magnitude |
+| SSR | `m_pTexHDRTargetMasked*` fp16 | source read is R11G11B10F; `min(color, 100×avgLum)` | **Yes**, except `fLum = 1.0f` in secondary viewports |
+| Probes | BC6H **unsigned** cube arrays | BC6UH (no negatives, ≤65504), baked to disk | Runtime yes; **baked assets no** — need rebake |
+| Particles | HDR fp16 (full + half res) | 8-bit vertex colour; `saturate` at `Particles.cfi:722`, `:982` | Partly — the ×0.1 factor is hardcoded in four places |
+| Clouds | HDR fp16; R11G11B10F shadows | reduced-range block present but `#define`-disabled | **Yes** (today) |
+| Sky | `m_pTexHDRTarget` fp16, **no clamps** | none | **No** — `Renderer.cpp:4007` vs `:4032` scale oppositely |
+
+**Three brightness levers already plumbed and currently inert:**
+`m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` (§C7, reaches sun / tiled lights / probes / clip volumes /
+volumetric fog); `PS_HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_MAX` (`FXConstantDefs.cfi:106`, reaches ~20
+forward/transparent shader sites); and `SkyDome_SkyBoxParams.z` (`Sky.cpp:146-148`, uploaded with
+no consumer — the lowest-risk place to inject a sky-only correction).
