+## Implications for a scene-referred ccam path
+
+### (a) The minimal set of places a ccam-only branch must touch
+
+1. **Pre-exposure injection — five existing sites, all currently multiplying by a hard-wired 1.0.**
+   `TiledLightVolumes.cpp:824-828`, `Common/RenderView.cpp:591` and `:599`,
+   `ClipVolumes.cpp:272`, `VolumetricFog.cpp:1043`. Driving
+   `CD3D9Renderer::m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` (`XRenderD3D9/DriverD3D.h:699`) from the ccam's
+   `ComputeManualEV100()` is the cheapest possible pre-exposure, and it needs **no new shader
+   code**. Caveats: it does *not* cover emissive materials (which bypass deferred entirely, §D9d),
+   the skybox (`Common/Renderer.cpp:4006-4032`), or forward transparents — those would need their
+   own multiply, or the exposure has to move to the tiled-shading write
+   (`TiledShading.cfi:1071`) plus the sky and forward paths.
+2. **The tone-map shader** — `HDRPostProcess.cfx`, `FilmMapping()` at `:818-846` and
+   `HDRToneMapSample` at `:867-872`. A ccam branch needs a new static flag alongside the existing
+   `%_RT_SAMPLE1..6` to replace `:838-844` (`max(cColor,0)` → Hable → `saturate` → sRGB) with a
+   baked ODT LUT sample, and to bypass `ComputeExposure` (`:801-816`) when the plugin supplies
+   exposure. Flags are assembled at `ToneMapping.cpp:78-91`; there are six `SAMPLE` bits in use,
+   so a seventh is available.
+3. **The exposure constant path** — `ToneMapping.cpp:114-131`. Today the only exposure input is
+   `HDREyeAdaptation` (`hdrSetupParams[3]` or `[4]`) plus the 1×1 luminance texture at slot 1;
+   a ccam exposure scalar would ride in as a new constant or reuse `HDREyeAdaptation.x == .y`.
+4. **`r_HDREyeAdaptationMode`** — default **2** (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1290`) routes to the
+   legacy Krawczyk branch and makes the plugin's existing `E3DPARAM_HDR_EYEADAPTATION_PARAMS`
+   writes inert. The ccam path must either force mode 1 or bypass both branches.
+5. **The ODT LUT** — the existing colour-chart hook (`HDRPostProcess.cfx:966-969` →
+   `PostEffectsLib.cfi:183-208`) is 16³ / 256×16 / R8G8B8A8 / `saturate`-domain and sits *after*
+   the sRGB encode. It is usable as an unchanged display-referred grade, but **not** as a
+   scene-referred ODT. A ccam ODT needs a new sampler and a new lookup helper (log-domain input,
+   ≥ 33³, ≥ fp16), or a shaper LUT in front of the existing one.
+6. **Sun shafts** — `SunShafts.cpp:36-43` must stop writing into `m_pTexDisplayTargetScaled[]`
+   (R10G10B10A2 UNORM) if shafts are to stay scene-referred, and the composite at
+   `HDRPostProcess.cfx:964` must move before the ODT rather than after it. Note also
+   `ToneMapping.cpp:138` `sunColor.Normalize();` — shaft brightness is decoupled from the sun
+   entirely, so a ccam exposure will not move it. That is a separate, pre-existing bug.
+6b. **`Renderer.cpp:4007` and `ShaderResources.h:107`** must be changed together if
+   `RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE` is ever touched — they apply reciprocal powers of the same
+   constant to two terms that are summed at `Renderer.cpp:4032`. Changing it alone diverges the
+   TOD skybox from material emittance by the **square** of the factor (§G16, §D9c).
+7. **The 709→AP1 conversion point and its dependants** — §F13e. At minimum
+   `GetLuminanceWeights()` (`CommonMath.cfi:128-131`) needs a ccam-conditional AP1 variant for the
+   four linear-HDR consumers: auto-exposure metering (`HDRPostProcess.cfx:743-753`), the HDR
+   saturation pivot (`:833`), the DOF highlight extraction (`DepthOfField.cfx:435/756/1105`), and
+   the firefly filter (`PostEffects.cfx:305-363`).
+8. **Nothing else, if the ccam path stays on the default feature set.** Volumetric fog is off by
+   default (`Cry3DEngine/cvars.cpp:100`), legacy fog is off by default
+   (`Cry3DEngine/EnvironmentPreset.cpp:261-262`), and SVOGI is off by default
+   (`Cry3DEngine/SVO/SceneTreeCVars.inl:211` → `D3D_SVO.cpp:1657`). Both subsystems carry
+   scale-dependent machinery that a pre-exposure would break (§G14 item 12, §G15 items 1–5), so
+   **the cheapest correct scope for a first ccam pass is to require them off** rather than to fix
+   them. If either is wanted later, §G14/§G15 list exactly what must change.
+9. **TAA needs no change while the ODT stays where the tone-map is.** PostAA runs entirely after
+   the ODT on `[0,1]` sRGB data (§B4, §H17), so a ccam exposure/ODT swap is invisible to it. It
+   only becomes a problem if the post chain is moved to scene-referred, at which point the UNORM
+   history buffer (`PostAA.cpp:627`), the `saturate` at `PostAA.cfx:178`, `:1064`, `:1185`, and the
+   absolute `0.02` thresholds (`PostAA.cfx:284`, `Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1507`) all become
+   invalid at once.
+
+### (b) Formats that must change
+
+| Target | Today | Why it must change | Where |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `m_pTexHDRTargetPrev[0..1]` | **R11G11B10F** | no sign bit; AP1 conversion produces negatives for saturated 709 colours; also the motion-blur and SSR input | `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:239-240` (change `nHDRQFormat` → `nHDRFormat`, or set `r_HDRTexFormat 2`) |
+| `m_pTexSceneTargetR11G11B10F[0..1]` | **R11G11B10F** | motion-blur input copy and lens-optics output | `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:243-244` |
+| `m_pTexHDRFinalBloom` | **R11G11B10F** | the bloom result itself | `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:246` |
+| `m_pTexWaterVolumeRefl[0..1]` | **R11G11B10F** | scene colour | `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:300-301` |
+| `m_pTexDisplayTargetSrc/Dst` | **R10G10B10A2 UNORM** | the tone-map output; any scene-referred post beyond the ODT is impossible while this clamps to `[0,1]` | `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:294-295` (`nLDRPFormat`) |
+| `m_pTexDisplayTargetScaled[0..2]` / `…Temp[0..1]` | **R10G10B10A2 UNORM** | the sun-shafts working set | `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:289-291`, `:297-298` |
+| PostAA `$PrevBackBuffer0/1` | **R16G16B16A16 UNORM** | only if post-AA is to run scene-referred | `PostAA.cpp:627-629`, `:641-642`, `:647-649` |
+| Colour chart | 256×16 **R8G8B8A8**, `[0,1]` domain | inadequate as an ODT (8-bit, 16³, clamped) | `ColorGrading.cpp:9`, `IColorGradingCtrl.h:22-24`, `PostEffectsLib.cfi:191` |
+| Swapchain | `DXGI_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM` | only if HDR output is wanted; the plumbing for `R16G16B16A16_FLOAT` exists at `SwapChain.cpp:59` but the whole cvar is `#if 0`-ed | `SwapChain.cpp:38-72`, `Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1161-1190`, `Common/RenderDisplayContext.h:98`, `:103` |
+
+Only if fog / SVOGI are in scope (both off by default — see (a) item 8):
+
+| Target | Today | Why | Where |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `m_pVolFogBufDensityColor` | **R11G11B10F** | fog albedo × density | `VolumetricFog.cpp:246`, `:330` |
+| `m_pVolFogBufEmissive` | **R11G11B10F** | the kcd/m² fog emission | `VolumetricFog.cpp:248`, `:332` |
+| SVO brick pools (all) | **R8G8B8A8** + the 4.0-ceiling RGBM codec | caps every bounce at 4.0 with 8-bit mantissa | `SceneTree.cpp:939`; `CommonSVO.cfi:142-146`, `:291-298` |
+| SVO RSM colour/normal maps | **R8G8B8A8** | no HDR headroom in the sun RSM | `D3D_SVO.cpp:1935`, `:1943`, `:1958`, `:1966` |
+| Cloud shadow 3D + shadow map | **R11G11B10F** | only if radiance is ever put in them | `VolumetricClouds.cpp:516`, `:612` |
+
+Formats that are **already adequate** and need no change: the SSR chain (always fp16 —
+`nHDRAFormat` cannot degrade, `GraphicsPipeline.cpp:229-241`), the cloud history targets
+(`VolumetricClouds.cpp:566-581`), the sky path (`Sky.cpp:41-45`, writing unclamped into the fp16
+HDR target), and the probe atlases (BC6UH, `TiledLightVolumes.cpp:80`) — though BC6H is
+*unsigned*, so AP1-converted probe content with negative channels would clip, and **every baked
+probe must be re-baked after any unit rescale** (§G16).
+
+The cheapest global lever is **`r_HDRTexFormat 2`** (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1192-1198`), which
+makes `GetHDRFormat(false, true)` return fp16 and so upgrades `HDRTargetPrev`,
+`SceneTargetR11G11B10F`, `HDRFinalBloom` and `WaterVolumeRefl` in one move. It does **not** touch
+the `nLDRPFormat` targets, the PostAA history, the fog volumes (which hardcode `eTF_R11G11B10F`
+rather than going through `GetHDRFormat`), or anything in SVOGI.
+
+### (c) Unknowns
+
+1. **What the ccam's exposure should multiply.** Pre-exposing lights (§C7) misses emissive
+   materials, the skybox and forward transparents. Whether to instead pre-expose at the
+   tiled-shading write plus three extra sites, or to keep exposure entirely at the tone-map, is a
+   design decision this audit cannot settle.
+2. **How to reconcile the π asymmetry** (§D9b) with an AP1 scene-referred convention. Both
+   options (fold 1/π into the diffuse BRDF, or drop it from `ConvertIlluminanceToLightColor` and
+   remove the three manual undos) change the look of every existing scene.
+3. **The 100× scale collision at `Common/Renderer.cpp:4032`** — whether it is a bug or an
+   intentional compensation could not be determined from the source; no comment addresses it.
+4. **The Nishita procedural sky's unit** (§D9c) is undocumented and does not reference
+   `RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE`. It cannot be placed on the photometric scale from source alone;
+   it would need empirical calibration.
+5. *(Resolved during the audit — kept here for the record.)* **Two static flags are free for the
+   tone-map technique.** The engine defines exactly seven, `HWSR_SAMPLE0..HWSR_SAMPLE6`
+   (`Common/Shaders/Shader.h:570-576`). `CToneMappingStage::Execute` sets SAMPLE1–SAMPLE6
+   (`ToneMapping.cpp:79-91`), but `HDRFinalScenePS` only *reads* SAMPLE1 (`HDRPostProcess.cfx:967`),
+   SAMPLE3 (`:954`), SAMPLE5 (`:963`) and SAMPLE6 (`:971`), plus SAMPLE4 inside `FilmMapping`
+   (`:824`). **SAMPLE2 is set by C++ and read nowhere** — the local vignette rework replaced the
+   gate with the `HDRVignetteParams.x` constant (`HDRPostProcess.cfx:927-934`), so the
+   `if (bVignettingEnabled)` at `ToneMapping.cpp:84-85` is dead. **SAMPLE0** is used by other
+   techniques in the same shader (`:142`, `:774`, `:1461`) but not by `HDRFinalPass`, so it is
+   free here too. A ccam ODT branch therefore has SAMPLE0 available immediately, and SAMPLE2
+   after removing the dead set.
+6. **Whether the RC can produce a float/high-bit-depth LUT texture** for a scene-referred ODT.
+   `rc.ini:348-354` `[ColorChart] colorspace=linear,linear` implies raw data, but no float DDS
+   chart preset exists in the shipped `rc.ini`; whether one can be added was not investigated.
+7. **The `r_HDRSwapChain` `#if 0` block's assumptions.** The TODO
+   (`Common/RendererCVars.cpp:1161`, `Common/SwapChain.cpp:40`) says the shader-side sRGB encode
+   must go first, but whether the rest of `CSwapChainBackedRenderDisplayContext` (back-buffer
+   proxies, `ResolveHighDynamicRangeDisplay`, the DX12 shim's `SetColorSpace1`) is actually
+   complete enough to be re-enabled was not verified — nothing exercises it today.
+8. **Whether any existing content depends on the `[0,1]` clamp** at `HDRPostProcess.cfx:841/871`
+   — e.g. UI drawn through `EFSLIST_AFTER_HDRPOSTPROCESS` (`SceneForward.cpp:1137-1167`) into the
+   now-unclamped display target.
+9. **Whether the volumetric-fog `×16` range shift** (`VolumeLighting.cfi:19`) was chosen for fp16
+   headroom, for the R11G11B10F volumes, or empirically — no comment explains it, so the correct
+   value under a rescaled unit system cannot be derived from source.
+10. **What the SVO radiance codec should be replaced with.** The 4.0 ceiling
+    (`CommonSVO.cfi:142-146`) is baked into an 8-bit pool format (`SceneTree.cpp:939`); whether a
+    wider codec, an `R11G11B10F` pool, or an exposure-tracking exponent is the right answer is a
+    design decision, and the memory cost of the pools was not measured here.
+11. **Whether SMAA_1TX's diagonals-only neighbourhood** (§H17 mechanism 1) is deliberate or a
+    long-standing oversight — the edge-adjacent taps are fetched in the TSAA branch only
+    (`PostAA.cfx:196-199`), and no comment addresses it. Likewise the `float3 → float` truncation
+    of the blend weight at `PostAA.cfx:258-259`.
+12. **Whether re-baking every environment probe is acceptable** if the ccam path rescales light
+    units. Baked probes are BC6UH on disk with no compensating multiplier
+    (`Code/Tools/RC/rc.ini:287`, `:312`; `TiledLightVolumes.cpp:80`), and
+    `m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` scales the probe *tint* but not the cubemap contents
+    (`TiledLightVolumes.cpp:824`, `:842`) — so using it as the pre-exposure hook double-applies to
+    probes. Whether to exclude probes from the hook or to compensate in the bake was not resolved.
+13. **Whether `PS_HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_MAX`** (`FXConstantDefs.cfi:106`, currently 1.0) is a safe
+    shader-side lever for the ~20 forward/transparent sites it already reaches. It is plumbed but
+    has never been exercised at a non-unity value in this tree, so its correctness is untested.
+14. **Whether the editor's forced `eAT_SMAA_1X`** (`PostAA.cpp:559-560`,
+    `// TODO: Support temporal AA in the editor`) matters for ccam work, which is largely
+    editor-driven: any temporal behaviour tuned in the viewport will differ in game mode.
