+# Scene-Referred Pipeline — Specification
+
+Status: approved for implementation, 2026-08-28. Branch `scene`, worktree `CRYENGINE_Scene`.
+Companion documents: `SceneReferredResearch.md` (read-only audit of CE 5.7.1, the factual basis of
+everything below), `scene-notes/STRUCTURE.md` (impact map, outside git), `scene-notes/research/`
+and `scene-notes/decisions/` (per-item notes, outside git). Working rules: root `CLAUDE.md`.
+
+This is a change of the same order as CE's own move to PBR. It is developed in isolation so that it
+can be abandoned at any time without a trace in `dev`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Goal
+
+Bring real high dynamic range into the engine render, such that:
+
+1. the image can be previewed on a Rec.709 display and the game can be played through it;
+2. the same data can later be written to high-dynamic-range formats (image sequences first;
+   HEVC is a bonus, not a requirement of this spec);
+3. adjusting the picture — in a virtual studio or in the game — feels like adjusting HDR /
+   wide-gamut scene data, never like adjusting a JPEG or an SDR video.
+
+Positioning: individuals and small teams, not the film industry. Align with industry practice at a
+small scale, thoroughly enough to avoid the pits others fell into (see §3).
+
+### Non-goals of this specification
+TAA rework for highlight flicker (separate item; see §7.9), HDR display output (swapchain), Log /
+ProRes / DNG encoders, the sensor / film-stock body model, the Program Monitor, live-action
+compositing tools. They build on this work and are specified later.
+
+---
+
+## 2. The one rule
+
+**Nothing between lighting and the last LUT may know that a display exists.** Exactly one
+transform — the ODT — maps scene luminance to display code values. Everything else (exposure,
+white balance, bloom, glare, DOF, grading) operates on "how much light is in the scene", in scene
+units (stops, Kelvin, cd/m²), never in [0,1].
+
+```
+lighting (Rec.709 linear, 1.0 = 10 000 cd/m²)
+  → pre-exposure (ccam EV100)                      scene-linear, exposed: 18 % grey = 0.18
+  → 3×3 Rec.709 → ACEScg (AP1, D60 via Bradford)   working space of the whole post chain, fp16, no clamps
+  → post effects in this space (bloom, DOF, ghosts, diffraction, halation, motion blur, SSR …)
+  → camera stage: white balance (Bradford), ND         still scene-linear
+  → grade stage: ASC CDL in ACEScct  +  Look LUT slot (LMT)
+  ─── EXPORT TAP: the buffer here is what gets written to EXR ───
+  → ODT: ACES 2.0 output transform, baked offline by OCIO into a 3D LUT (sRGB / Rec.709 100 nit)
+  → dither → back buffer
+```
+
+With the CinematicCamera (ccam) component inactive the engine runs its stock path, byte-identical.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Precedents followed and pits avoided
+
+We do not invent where a trodden path exists.
+
+| Topic | Follow | Avoid |
+|---|---|---|
+| Units & exposure | Frostbite (Lagarde & de Rousiers 2014): photometric units, EV100, pre-exposure into fp16; UE `r.UsePreExposure` | keeping raw radiance in fp16 (sun overflows), engine-owned eye adaptation as the exposure |
+| Working space | ACEScg (AP1, D60), the VFX/DI standard; sRGB ⊂ AP1 so unsigned formats stay valid | a private "D65 AP1" that makes exported EXRs non-standard |
+| Grading | ASC CDL in ACEScct (Resolve, Baselight, Nuke interchange), LMT as a `.cube` in log space | grading in display space after the tone map (UE's post-tonemap LUT asset) |
+| Display transform | ACES 2.0 output transforms via OCIO 2.4, baked to a 3D LUT with a log shaper; UE's per-frame `CombineLUTs` idea for interactivity | ACES 1.x RRT hue skews; a hand-tuned tone curve baked in shader code with hidden "corrections" (UE Blue Correction / Expand Gamut) |
+| Working-space discipline | explicit conversion at one point, AP1-aware luminance weights | implicit sRGB assumptions scattered through systems (UE pre-5.1) |
+| Export | OpenEXR half, ACEScg primaries (ACES container convention) | 8-bit captures of the back buffer |
+
+---
+
+## 4. Decision register
+
+Agreed with the user on 2026-08-28. Each item's implementation still goes through a
+`scene-notes/decisions/` note with ≥2 (ideally ≥3) usable approaches.
+
+| # | Decision | Rationale / precedent |
+|---|---|---|
+| D1 | Scenes for the ReC path are lit with real light ratios (≥10 stops sun/shade). "Engine still usable" is a code-level guarantee (stock path byte-identical), not "both paths look the same on one scene". We ship preprocessing/defaults so users do not hit physics pitfalls out of the box. | audit §D10: default sun vs default point light is 1.9 stops |
+| D2 | Game auto-exposure is the **camera's AUTO mode**, implemented in ccam, acting on scene-linear, with on/off, lock and compensation. Engine eye adaptation is bypassed. | real cameras; cleaner than the two `r_HDREyeAdaptationMode` branches |
+| D3 | Exposure is applied on the **light side** (pre-exposure) through the existing `m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` sites, extended to emissive, skybox and forward/transparent paths; env probes are excluded from the tint hook and scaled on content instead. | audit §C7; Frostbite/UE pre-exposure |
+| D4 | The sun/sky ÷π asymmetry is unified: all lights are radiometric, 1/π lives in the diffuse BRDF; the three manual undos go away. ReC scenes are re-lit; probes re-baked. | audit §D9b |
+| D5 | Working space is **standard ACEScg** (AP1, D60) with a Bradford-adapted Rec.709→AP1 matrix. | exported EXRs must be standard ACES |
+| D6 | After pre-exposure, a correctly exposed 18 % reflector is **0.18** in the HDR target (ACES convention). The calibration constant (CE's `ComputeExposure` C=330 vs the ISO 12.5/100 form) is settled in the exposure research note. | ODT LUT input domain is then standard, no private offsets |
+| D7 | AUTO metering reuses the engine's luminance-measure pass (pre-exposure-aware); smoothing, metering modes (average / centre-weighted / spot) and limits belong to ccam. | reuse over reinvention |
+| D8 | LUTs enter the engine as **`.cube` text files parsed by ccam** into fp16 3D textures (≥33³), bypassing the RC. Each frame a compute pass combines WB + CDL + LMT + ODT into one LUT (UE `CombineLUTs` structure); exposure is *not* in the LUT. | RC cannot make float LUTs (audit E11/F); Resolve's native LUT format |
+| D9 | With ccam active the entire stock LDR post stage (colour chart, saturation/contrast, vignette, sharpen, grain) is skipped; after the ODT only dither remains. Wanted effects are re-created before the ODT in scene units (vignette = lens, grain = sensor). Users will notice stock sliders going inert — accepted. | audit §C8: the LDR stage is the source of the "JPEG feel" |
+| D10 | The no-grade default is **pure ACES 2.0**; no hidden "ReC look". If a house look is ever wanted it is a visible, deletable LMT. | the opposite of UE's baked corrections |
+| D11 | Our own effects' thresholds (bloom, DOF highlight extraction, glare family, firefly filter) become exposure-relative (relative to 0.18), which is the physical behaviour. The FFT glare `Streak Amount` default 50 (a compensation for clamped lights) returns to the physical 1. | audit §B3 |
+| D12 | EXR export of the pre-ODT buffer is part of **this** stage, as the acceptance instrument: Resolve applying the same ACES 2.0 ODT to the EXR must match the engine view. | objective proof of alignment |
+| D13 | Effects that break under the new units/formats (volumetric fog, SVOGI, sun shafts, clouds, particles…) are **not disabled**. They run, break visibly, and get fixed. | user rule: hiding breakage ships pits |
+| D14 | ccam forces the exposure path it needs regardless of `r_HDREyeAdaptationMode` (engine default 2 silently ignores ccam's EV writes today; the sample project happens to set 1). | audit §C5 |
+
+---
+
+## 5. Conventions
+
+- **Engine luminance unit** stays `1.0 = 10 000 cd/m²` (`RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE`). We fix the six
+  inconsistencies (audit §D9f), we do not change the scale.
+- **Pre-exposure**: `scale = 1 / (L_sat(EV100))` with `L_sat = 1.2 · 2^EV100` in cd/m² (ISO
+  saturation-based, q = 0.65), converted to engine units. EV100 from ccam (manual: T-stop,
+  shutter, ISO, ND; auto: metered) — the exact constant per D6.
+- **Working space** from the HDR target onward: ACEScg linear, fp16 (`RGBA16F`), no clamps.
+  `r_HDRTexFormat 2` (fp16 satellites) is forced while ccam is active. Fog volumes and any
+  hardcoded `R11G11B10F` are converted as they are reached (D13).
+- **Luminance** in the working space uses AP1 weights (`GetLuminanceWeights()` gains a ccam-conditional
+  AP1 variant; audit §F13b lists the four HDR consumers).
+- **Grading space**: ACEScct. CDL = slope, offset, power (per channel) + saturation, ASC order.
+- **Display transform**: ACES 2.0 Output Transform, sRGB / Rec.709, 100 nit, D65 sim, baked by OCIO
+  2.4 (ACES Studio config) into a `.cube` with an ACEScct shaper. Other outputs (P3, Rec.2020 PQ,
+  Log) are just other bakes — later.
+- **Master switch**: `r_SceneReferred` (0/1), set by ccam on activation and restored on
+  deactivation, like the existing `r_DepthOfFieldLensModel` pattern. Everything in this spec is
+  gated by it; with 0 the renderer is byte-identical to stock.
+- **Naming**: cvars `r_SceneReferred*`; ccam parameters under "Exposure", "White Balance",
+  "Grade", "Look", "Output" groups; Schematyc member names `[A-Za-z0-9_]+`.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Work items
+
+Each item = research note(s) on the CE code it touches → decisions note → implementation (Opus)
+→ review (Fable) → commit on `scene` → `STRUCTURE.md` update. Order is dependency order; items
+within a stage may interleave.
+
+### Stage S0 — foundations
+- `r_SceneReferred` master switch; ccam sets/restores it; D14 exposure-path forcing.
+- Force `r_HDRTexFormat 2` under the switch; verify no `R11G11B10F` remains on the colour path
+  except the ones scheduled in S8.
+- Byte-identity harness: a RenderDoc / screenshot comparison of stock vs `scene` build with the
+  switch off (used at every review).
+- Touches CE code: `RendererCVars`, `GraphicsPipeline.cpp` format selection, `ToneMapping.cpp`.
+
+### Stage S1 — exposure
+- Pre-exposure from ccam EV100 through `m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` (five sites) + emissive
+  (`Illum.cfx`, `MultiLayeredMaterials.cfx` kcd literal → shared constant) + skybox
+  (`Renderer.cpp:4007/4032`, incl. the 100× collision) + forward/transparent lever
+  (`PS_HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_MAX` sites) ; probes excluded from the tint hook.
+- Luminance measure made pre-exposure-aware; ccam AUTO mode (D2, D7): modes, smoothing, lock,
+  compensation, limits; manual mode unchanged in UI, now physically absolute.
+- ND filter enters the same EV.
+- Acceptance: opening 3 stops brings back cloud detail from "white"; closing 3 stops keeps shadow
+  content; a 1-px emissive at 200 kcd/m² does not overflow fp16; AUTO walks indoors→outdoors like a
+  camera, not like eye adaptation.
+
+### Stage S2 — units
+- π unification (D4); `ConvertIlluminanceToLightColor`, `TimeOfDay.cpp:471`, the three undos.
+- Sun shafts: `sunColor.Normalize()` removed; shafts computed pre-ODT in fp16 (moved out of the
+  `DisplayTargetScaled` UNORM set); composite before the ODT.
+- Physical TOD/sky/sun defaults for ReC scenes ("preprocessing", D1): a preset with real ratios
+  and a sane default EV so a new scene opens looking right. Nishita sky calibrated empirically
+  against the skybox path.
+- Probe re-bake procedure documented; bake exposure handled so probes carry unexposed radiance.
+- Acceptance: sun / shade ratio measured ≥ 10 stops in a default ReC scene; sun shafts follow
+  exposure and ND; probes match direct lighting after re-bake.
+
+### Stage S3 — working space
+- 709→ACEScg at the HDR-target entry of the post chain (exact point per decisions note: after
+  deferred+forward resolve, before any post effect reads it).
+- AP1 luminance weights for: exposure metering, HDR saturation pivot, DOF highlight extraction,
+  firefly filter (audit §F13b).
+- Every post effect audited for `saturate` / clamps on colour (audit §B3 list) and cleared under
+  the switch where it clips colour data (not masks/weights).
+- Acceptance: a saturated red light bloomed and pushed +2 stops stays red (no hue rotation, no
+  channel clip); AP1-encoded negatives never appear (sRGB ⊂ AP1) — verified by a debug readback.
+
+### Stage S4 — display transform
+- `.cube` parser + fp16 3D texture upload (ccam side); shaper/LUT sampling helper in
+  `HDRPostProcess.cfx`; new static flag on `HDRFinalPass` (SAMPLE0 free; SAMPLE2 dead) selecting
+  the ODT branch and bypassing `ComputeExposure`/`FilmMapping`.
+- Per-frame combined LUT (compute): WB (Bradford, Kelvin + tint) → ACEScct → CDL → LMT → ODT.
+- `DisplayTarget` fp16 under the switch; LDR stage skipped; dither pass; colour chart bypassed;
+  HUD/`EFSLIST_AFTER_HDRPOSTPROCESS` verified.
+- OCIO bake tool: `tools/ocio-bake/` (uv-managed Python, `PyOpenColorIO` 2.4, ACES Studio config)
+  producing the shipped ODT `.cube`s; documented so anyone can regenerate them.
+- Acceptance: with no CDL/LMT the view equals OCIO's own render of the same EXR through the same
+  view (D12); switching ODT files changes only the display, never the EXR.
+
+### Stage S5 — camera grading controls
+- ccam: White Balance (Kelvin, tint), CDL (slope/offset/power/saturation), LMT `.cube` slot,
+  ODT selection; all in scene units, all live (per-frame LUT rebuild).
+- `.cdl` import/export is a stretch goal here (cheap, high interchange value).
+- Acceptance: WB 5600 K → 3200 K keeps clipped highlights neutral; saturation push does not hue
+  shift; CDL values round-trip with Resolve.
+
+### Stage S6 — export
+- EXR writer (tinyexr, half, ACEScg primaries, chromaticities attribute, camera metadata
+  attributes) hooked where `WriteTIF` lives; a capture cvar/command on the pre-ODT buffer;
+  frame-sequence naming.
+- Acceptance (the stage's proof): EXR + same ODT in Resolve == engine view.
+
+### Stage S7 — effect re-thresholding (D11)
+- Bloom threshold, DOF highlight extraction, halation, analytic streaks, FFT glare source, ghosts,
+  front-filter PSF: thresholds expressed relative to mid-grey; `Streak Amount` default → 1;
+  ConsoleReference/README updated.
+- Acceptance: glare and bloom scale with aperture/ND continuously; no effect "pops in" at a
+  particular stop.
+
+### Stage S8 — breakage sweep (D13)
+- Run with volumetric fog, SVOGI, clouds, particles, water, sun shafts **on**. Log each breakage
+  (`scene-notes/log.md`), fix at the root: fog `×16` shift and `R11G11B10F` volumes; SVO radiance
+  codec (4.0 cap, 8-bit pools, `pow`) and RSM formats; anything else found.
+- Acceptance: every stock feature renders sensibly at the ReC scene's light ratios.
+
+### Later (own specs)
+TAA on scene-referred data (luminance-weighted resolve; also the SMAA_1TX diagonal-only
+neighbourhood and the red-channel-only blend weight, audit §H17); HDR swapchain; Log/ProRes/DNG;
+sensor/film model; Program Monitor.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Notes carried from the audit that shape the work
+
+1. The tone map is already photometric (ISO-100 model, `1.0 = 10 000 cd/m²`); we keep the unit and
+   fix the six breaks (audit §D9f).
+2. The hard wall is the tone-map output `R10G10B10A2 UNORM`; everything after it assumes [0,1].
+   Keeping the ODT at the tone-map position means PostAA still sees [0,1] data — that is why TAA is
+   out of scope here.
+3. `m_fAdaptedSceneScaleLBuffer` exists at five sites and is always 1.0 — the pre-exposure hook.
+4. `SAMPLE0` is free on `HDRFinalPass`; `SAMPLE2` is set but never read (dead vignette gate).
+5. Colour is hard-coded Rec.709 throughout; the single 709→2020 matrix is unused and broken.
+6. Capture is 8-bit from the back buffer; `WriteTIF` is the only float writer.
+7. Volumetric fog and SVOGI are off by default but carry scale-dependent machinery; per D13 they
+   are exercised on, not avoided.
+8. Editor viewport forces SMAA_1X (no temporal pass) — temporal behaviour must be judged in game
+   mode.
+9. Probes are BC6UH (unsigned) with no compensating multiplier; the tint hook double-applies.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Acceptance for the whole stage (plain language)
+
+1. ccam off → engine byte-identical to stock (RenderDoc/screenshot diff clean).
+2. Open the aperture 3 stops → clouds outside the window gain detail instead of staying white;
+   close 3 stops → shadows keep content.
+3. WB 5600 K → 3200 K → highlights stay white, the picture warms as a whole; no global tint.
+4. Push saturation hard → red lights stay red, blue sky stays blue; no yellow/orange or cyan drift.
+5. Sun glare / sun shafts follow aperture and ND continuously; nothing appears suddenly at one stop.
+6. Export EXR → Resolve with the same ODT → same picture as the engine.
+7. Stock colour chart / saturation / vignette sliders do nothing while ccam is on (expected).
+8. Volumetric fog, SVOGI, clouds, particles render sensibly in a ReC-lit scene (after S8).
+
+---
+
+## 9. Process reminders
+
+- No research note → no change. No decisions note (≥2 usable approaches) → no implementation.
+- Update `scene-notes/STRUCTURE.md` per touched node; append to `scene-notes/log.md` per session.
+- Commit per reviewed step on `scene`; the public snapshot is synced only when the user closes the
+  stage. `dev` is never touched by this work until the user merges.
+- Abandonment: `git worktree remove CRYENGINE_Scene`, delete branch `scene`; `dev` and the
+  `stock-pipeline` snapshot are untouched.
